# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Trusted-Header SSO Bridge:**"
msgstr "**Most za varno glavo SSO:**"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Trusted-Header SSO Bridge:**   When the oauth2-proxy SSO flavor is active, Snipe-IT's native `loginViaRemoteUser()` is enabled via the `Setting` model (`login_remote_user_enabled`, `login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME`). nginx gates `/login` through oauth2-proxy/Keycloak and injects the verified `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username` header, which Snipe-IT matches against `users.username` (the user must pre-exist and be activated — sync them via LDAP) to mint a native `snipeit_session`. Visitors without a matching activated user silently fall through to the normal login form (no error). The password/LDAP login form stays available as a fallback (`login_common_disabled = 0`), and the in-app logout is redirected to the central OIDC end-session URL."
msgstr "**Most za varno glavo SSO:** Ko oauth2-proxy SSO okus je aktiven, Snipe-IT je domačin `loginViaRemoteUser()` omogočen preko `Setting` model (`login_remote_user_enabled`, `login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME`). ginx vrata `/login` skozi oauth2proksi/Keycloak in injicira preverjeno `X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username` glava, ki se ujema s Snipe-IT `users.username` (uporabnik mora vnaprej obstajati in biti aktiviran – sinhronizirati jih mora prek LDAP) za kovanje domačina `snipeit_session`. Obiskovalci brez ujemajočega se aktiviranega uporabnika tiho padejo na običajen prijavni obrazec (brez napake). Geslo / LDAP prijavni obrazec ostane na voljo kot rezervni (`login_common_disabled = 0`), in odjava v aplikaciji je preusmerjena na osrednji končni URL OIDC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Trusted-header SSO bridge:** Establishes the owner session from the oauth2-proxy identity (see below)."
msgstr "**Most za zanesljivo glavo SSO:** Ustanovi lastniško sejo iz oauth2-proksidna identiteta (glej spodaj)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Twenty-four roles' audit entries contradicted their own metadata** the first time the classification lint ran, nine of them shipping an adapter while the list called them untried candidates."
msgstr "**Štiriindvajset vpisov v zvezi z revizijo vlog je bilo v nasprotju z njihovimi lastnimi metapodatki** Ko je prvič potekala klasifikacija, jih je devet poslalo adapter, medtem ko jih je seznam imenoval neizkušene kandidate."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Two proofs were vacuous.** Flowise tool-name verification compared against a hardcoded empty list, and every role-local MCP spec gated itself on the service flag, so a surface that kept serving after being switched off was indistinguishable from one never deployed. Both now fail when they should."
msgstr "**Dva dokaza sta bila prazna.** Pretočno preverjanje imena orodja v primerjavi s težko kodiranim praznim seznamom, in vsaka vloga-lokalna Spec se je začrtala na zastavi storitve, tako da je površina, ki je služila po izklopu, bila nerazločna od tiste, ki ni bila nikoli uporabljena. Obema zdaj spodleti, ko bi morala."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Two strategies decide among the survivors, and `services.litellm.router_strategy` picks one.** Both run behind the same filter and behind decision 7's locality restriction; they differ only in what ranks the routes that are left."
msgstr "**Dve strategiji se odločata med preživelimi in `services.litellm.router_strategy` Izbere enega.** Oba tečeta za istim filtrom in za odločitvijo 7Lokalna omejitev; razlikujejo se samo po tem, kaj uvršča preostale poti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Two-layer tool policy:** Home Assistant offers no per-tool filter of its own; enabling the Assist API always publishes its actuating intents (`HassTurnOn`, `HassTurnOff`, the todo-list writers). The role names those in `tools.mutating`, and `mutating_tools_enabled: false` withholds them from every client's include list, so an agent is offered the read tools only. Entity exposure bounds the rest: the role exposes no entity to Assist, and making the hub actuate anything is an explicit operator step per entity."
msgstr "**Dvoslojna politika orodja:** Domov Pomočnik ponuja brez lastnega filtra na orodje; omogoča pomoč API vedno objavlja svoje namere (`HassTurnOn`, `HassTurnOff`, pisci todolistov). Vlogo imena tistih v `tools.mutating`, in `mutating_tools_enabled: false` Odreka jih seznamu strank, zato se agentu ponudi samo bralno orodje. Izpostavljenost subjekta je vezana na ostalo: vloga ne izpostavlja nobenega subjekta pomoči, in da vozlišče sproži vse, je izrecen korak upravljavca na subjekt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Two-layer tool policy:** Home Assistant offers no per-tool filter of its own; enabling the Assist API always publishes its actuating intents (``HassTurnOn``, ``HassTurnOff``, the todo-list writers). The role names those in ``tools.mutating``, and ``mutating_tools_enabled: false`` withholds them from every client’s include list, so an agent is offered the read tools only. Entity exposure bounds the rest: the role exposes no entity to Assist, and making the hub actuate anything is an explicit operator step per entity."
msgstr "**Dvoslojna politika orodja:** Domov Pomočnik ponuja brez lastnega filtra na orodje; omogoča pomoč API vedno objavlja svoje namere (``HassTurnOn``, ``HassTurnOff``, pisci todolistov). Vlogo imena tistih v ``tools.mutating``, in ``mutating_tools_enabled: false`` jih odreka seznamu vseh strank, zato se agentu ponudi samo bralno orodje. Izpostavljenost subjekta je vezana na ostalo: vloga ne izpostavlja nobenega subjekta pomoči, in da vozlišče sproži vse, je izrecen korak upravljavca na subjekt."

# translated-by: libretranslate
