# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**joomla local-login fallback spec** — `test-oidc-fallback.js:52` (the `?fallback=local` emergency hatch: local Joomla admin form login must reach the control panel). Root cause UNCONFIRMED. It is independent of the fixed OIDC-login spec: the fallback path short-circuits before the plugin's server-side discovery, so the committed `extra_hosts` fix does not cover it. The `secure => true` sticky-cookie hypothesis was rejected (`.onion` is a potentially-trustworthy origin and the e2e Firefox sets `dom.securecontext.allowlist_onions`, so Secure cookies are accepted over plain-http onion). Next step when it fails again post-fix: isolate the post-submit URL — Keycloak redirect (cookie lost) vs. form reject vs. slow control-panel render."
msgstr "**joomla lokalno-login rezervni spektr** — `test-oidc-fallback.js:52` (o `?fallback=local` zasilna loputa: lokalna Joomla admin oblika prijava mora doseči nadzorno ploščo). Root vzrok nepoškodovan. To je neodvisno od fiksne OIDC- login spec: zasilna pot kratek stiki pred odkritjem strežnika plugin, tako da je `extra_hosts` fiks ne pokriva. – `secure => true` hipoteza o lepljivem piškotu je bila zavrnjena (`.onion` je potencialno zanesljiv izvor in2e Firefox kompleti `dom.securecontext.allowlist_onions`, zato so varni piškotki sprejeti na ravni http čebula). Naslednji korak, ko ne uspe ponovno post-fix: izolirati post-predloži URL — Keycloak preusmeritev (piškotek izgubljen) vs. oblika zavrne vs. počasen nadzor-panel izris."

