# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Because that grant is irreversible once the container starts, the checks run inside the agent role before it deploys, not afterwards in this role: the agent is a shared service, so the service loader brings it up in the constructor stage while ``svc-ai`` roles only run at the following step. A check placed here would sit behind the deployment it exists to prevent."
msgstr "Ker je ta dotacija nepovratna, ko se posoda začne, preverjanja potekajo znotraj vloge zastopnika, preden se začne uporabljati, ne pozneje v tej vlogi: agent je skupna storitev, zato jo servisni nakladalnik dvigne v fazi konstruktorja, medtem ko ``svc-ai`` vloge potekajo le v naslednjem koraku. Ček, ki je postavljen tukaj, bi stal za razporedom, ki ga je treba preprečiti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Because that grant is irreversible once the container starts, the checks run inside the agent role before it deploys, not afterwards in this role: the agent is a shared service, so the service loader brings it up in the constructor stage while `svc-ai` roles only run at the following step. A check placed here would sit behind the deployment it exists to prevent."
msgstr "Ker je ta dotacija nepovratna, ko se posoda začne, preverjanja potekajo znotraj vloge zastopnika, preden se začne uporabljati, ne pozneje v tej vlogi: agent je skupna storitev, zato jo servisni nakladalnik dvigne v fazi konstruktorja, medtem ko `svc-ai` vloge potekajo le v naslednjem koraku. Ček, ki je postavljen tukaj, bi stal za razporedom, ki ga je treba preprečiti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Because the lookup emits ``$(...)`` shell syntax, callers MUST use the ``ansible.builtin.shell`` module (not ``command``) for the surrounding ``container exec`` invocation. A companion lint rule enforces this."
msgstr "Zato, ker pogled oddaja ``$(...)`` sintaksa lupin, klicarji MORAjo uporabljati ``ansible.builtin.shell`` modul (ni ``command``) za okolico ``container exec`` invokacija. To uveljavlja pravilo spremljevalca."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Because the pins use the same `(repository, ref)` shape as every other `meta/services.yml`, the existing `update-repository-refs` CI job discovers them on its own: it resolves the newest semver tag of each repository via `git ls-remote --tags` and opens a pull request with the bump. Upgrading a linter is therefore a reviewed commit, not a surprise."
msgstr "Ker igle uporabljajo enako. `(repository, ref)` oblika kot vsaka druga oblika `meta/services.yml`, obstoječe `update-repository-refs` Delo CI jih odkrije samostojno: reši najnovejšo semver oznako vsakega skladišča preko `git ls-remote --tags` in odpre prošnjo za poteg z buško. Nadgradnja interja je zato pregledana zaveza, ne presenečenje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Because the pins use the same ``(repository, ref)`` shape as every other ``meta/services.yml``, the existing ``update-repository-refs`` CI job discovers them on its own: it resolves the newest semver tag of each repository via ``git ls-remote --tags`` and opens a pull request with the bump. Upgrading a linter is therefore a reviewed commit, not a surprise."
msgstr "Ker igle uporabljajo enako. ``(repository, ref)`` oblika kot vsaka druga oblika ``meta/services.yml``, obstoječe ``update-repository-refs`` Delo CI jih odkrije samostojno: reši najnovejšo semver oznako vsakega skladišča preko ``git ls-remote --tags`` in odpre prošnjo za poteg z buško. Nadgradnja interja je zato pregledana zaveza, ne presenečenje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Because the same variant can run several times in one sweep, the onion state is part of what identifies a job: it is in the job label (`🧅` vs `🌐`) and in every artifact name. Two jobs uploading under one artifact name is a conflict, not an overwrite. The distro, filesystem and architecture glyphs follow it in the label (`🐳🧅🌀🦓🦾`), so a title says which combination died without opening the job."
msgstr "Ker lahko ista varianta večkrat teče v enem pregledu, je čebulno stanje del tega, kar označuje delo: je v oznaki delovnega mesta (`🧅` vs `🌐`) In v vsakem imenu artefakta. Dve nalogi, ki se nalagata pod enim imenom artefakta, sta spor, ne nadomestitev. Distro, datotečni sistem in arhitekturni glifi mu sledijo v oznaki (`🐳🧅🌀🦓🦾`)V naslovu piše, katera kombinacija je umrla brez službe."

