# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Databases travel as sql dumps, not as a file tree (`--dump-only-sql`), so they have their own recover leg: `recover database <generation>`, which `recover full` plans right after the volume steps. That leg is the one part of the chain that cannot run on a bare host: a dump is replayed through `docker exec`, so the database service has to be deployed and up, with its consumers stopped. The engine of a dump is resolved from the consuming role's `meta/services.yml` service key in `utils/recovery/databases.py` — the same value the backup seed used — and a replay refuses to run while a consumer of that database is up, because `--empty` pre-cleans the schema and a booting consumer would recreate it underneath the replay."
msgstr "Podatkovne baze potujejo kot odlagališča sql, ne kot datotečno drevo (`--dump-only-sql`), tako da imajo svoje okrevanje nogo: `recover database <generation>`, ki `recover full` načrtuje takoj po korakih glasnosti. Ta noga je edini del verige, ki ne more teči na golem gostitelju: smetišče se ponovno predvaja `docker exec`, tako da je treba storitev baze podatkov in navzgor, s svojimi potrošniki ustaviti. Motor smetišča se reši iz vloge potrošnega `meta/services.yml` servisni ključ v `utils/recovery/databases.py` – enaka vrednost uporabljenega rezervnega semena – in ponovitev zavrne delovanje, medtem ko je potrošnik te baze podatkov, ker `--empty` Predhodno čiščenje sheme in zagon potrošnik bi ga poustvarili pod ponovitev."

