# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Still open: MCP calls carrying that identity, and the obstacle is upstream rather than a piece of this platform nobody wrote yet. [ADR 0003](../architecture/decisions/0003-mcp-surface-per-provider.md) already fixes the bar: `auth_subject: user` may be set only after the exact client and server prove authorization-code or token-exchange behaviour, token refresh, audience binding, revocation and expiry. No MCP provider deployed here clears it — every server role authenticates as one `service_account`, because that is what its upstream offers — so `auth_subject: user` has nothing to resolve against. Meeting the bar means a provider gaining per-user OAuth upstream, not a credential model this repository can add on its own."
msgstr "Še vedno odprta: MCP klice, ki nosijo to identiteto, in ovira je v toku navzgor in ne del te platforme, ki ga še nihče ni napisal. [ADR 0003](../architecture/decisions/0003-mcp-surface-per-provider.md) že popravlja vrstico: `auth_subject: user` se lahko nastavi šele po tem, ko točen odjemalec in strežnik dokažeta obnašanje avtorizacije ali izmenjave žetonov, žetonsko osvežitev, vezavo občinstva, preklic in prenehanje veljavnosti. Noben ponudnik MCP ga ne počisti – vsaka vloga strežnika potrdi kot eno `service_account`, ker je to tisto, kar njena gornja ponudba – tako `auth_subject: user` Nima se proti čemu boriti. Srečanje z barom pomeni, da ponudnik pridobiva na uporabnika OAuth v toku navzgor, ne pa da lahko sam doda model zaupanja."

