# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Tests 🧪"
msgstr "Preskusi 🧪"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Thank you for contributing to a safe and inclusive Infinito.Nexus community!"
msgstr "Hvala, ker ste prispevali k varnemu in vključujočemu Infinito.Nexus skupnost!"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That choice is wrong in two directions at once. A prompt that needs a large context window reaches a model that cannot hold it, which is how [`web-app-hermes`](../../roles/web-app-hermes/) answers HTTP 500 when the agent model declares fewer than 64000 tokens. And a one-line factual question reaches whatever the deploy happened to pick, which is usually the largest model available."
msgstr "Ta izbira je napačna v dveh smereh naenkrat. Poziv, ki potrebuje veliko okno konteksta doseže model, ki ga ne more držati, tako [`web-app-hermes`](../../roles/web-app-hermes/) odgovori HTTP 500 če model zastopnika navaja manj kot 64000 Žetoni. In enovrstično stvarno vprašanje pride do tega, kar se je zgodilo, da so izbrali, kar je običajno največji model na voljo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That contract is wrong for one class of failure. When a value could not be measured and substituting one would be a guess, silence turns a loud stop into a wrong number nobody sees. Such a failure raises from here and every render layer re-raises it untouched."
msgstr "Ta pogodba je napačna za en razred neuspeha. Ko vrednosti ni bilo mogoče izmeriti in bi bila zamenjava ugibanja, tišina spremeni glasen postanek v napačno številko, ki je nihče ne vidi. Takšna napaka se dvigne od tukaj in vsaka plast jo ponovno dvigne nedotaknjeno."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That file brings the client to its desired MCP state from scratch, so the same file serves the role's own run and this one. `tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py` fails when a client role lacks it."
msgstr "Ta datoteka prinaša odjemalca v želeno MCP stanje iz nič, tako da ista datoteka služi lastni vlogi in ta. `tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py` propade, če stranka nima vloge."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That file brings the client to its desired MCP state from scratch, so the same file serves the role’s own run and this one. ``tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py`` fails when a client role lacks it."
msgstr "Ta datoteka prinaša odjemalec v želeno stanje MCP iz nič, tako da ista datoteka služi vlogi lastno delovanje in ta. ``tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_client_entrypoint.py`` propade, če stranka nima vloge."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is also what a retrigger replays: `--failed` reads the glyphs off the failed job's title and writes them back as a token, so the row comes back in the mode, onion state, distribution and architecture it died on rather than on whatever the rotation would pick next. The architecture is replayed because it is the machine the job ran on, not a preference it could fall back from. The filesystem is deliberately left out. A title states the kind the matrix *assigned*, which a deploy is allowed to fall back from, so pinning it would both misstate what the job ran on and turn the kind into a demand, failing the retrigger on the very condition the fallback absorbs."
msgstr "To je tudi tisto, kar retrigger ponovi: `--failed` prebere glife z naslova neuspešnega dela in jih zapiše nazaj kot žeton, tako da se vrsta vrne v načinu, stanju čebule, distribuciji in arhitekturi, na kateri je zamrla, namesto na tem, kar bi rotacija izbrala. Arhitektura je ponovno predvajana, ker je to stroj, na katerem je delo delovalo, ne pa preferenca, iz katere bi lahko padla. Datotečni sistem je namerno izpuščen. Naslov navaja vrsto matrice *dodeljena*, ki je uporaba dovoljeno, da se umaknejo iz, tako pinning bi tako napačno, kaj je delo tekel na in spremeniti vrsto v povpraševanje, ne uspe ponovno sprožiti pod pogojem, da rezervni absorbira."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is what stops the supervisor flow rather than effort. Flowise reaches an MCP server over the container network, and a stdio server has no address there: the client spawns and owns the process, so a shared endpoint two consumers could hold at once does not exist, and the deploy-time contract probe would consume the only session. Wrapping each agent in a stdio-to-HTTP bridge would put an unreviewed process on the platform's most privileged path — an agent with tool access — to work around a transport upstream has not shipped, which is the workaround this project refuses. Re-review when either upstream serves MCP over HTTP."
msgstr "To je tisto, kar ustavi tok nadzornika, namesto truda. Flowise doseže strežnik MCP preko omrežja zabojnikov, strežnik stdio pa tam nima naslova: odjemalec drsti in je lastnik procesa, tako da skupna končna točka, ki bi jo lahko imeli dva potrošnika naenkrat, ne obstaja, pogodbena sonda za razporeditev pa bi porabila edino sejo. Zavijanje vsakega agenta v most stdio-to-HTTP bi postavilo nepregledan proces na najbolj privilegirano pot platforme – agenta z dostopom do orodja – za delo okoli prevoza v smeri proti toku ni bilo odposlano, kar je delo v zvezi s tem projektom zavrača. Ponovni pregled, ko katera koli od zgoraj navedenih uporablja MCP nad HTTP."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is why the repo favors:"
msgstr "Zato je repo naklonjen:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is why the repo has:"
msgstr "Zato ima repo:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That is why you will find host work in `sys-*` roles and app work in `web-app-*` roles instead of one giant deployment script."
msgstr "Zato boste našli delo gostitelja v `sys-*` Vloge in aplikacije delo v `web-app-*` Vloge namesto enega velikega scenarija."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That last step is deliberately the deployed [`sys-ctl-hlth-container` script](../../../sys-ctl-hlth-container/files/shell/script.sh) rather than a check of the drill's own: it is what watches the host in production, it knows swarm services, and it dumps 200 log lines per sick container. It is invoked as a script, not as its systemd unit — the unit's `OnFailure` starts the soft-repair service, and a drill that repairs what it found has stopped measuring. It cannot replace the drill's own wait either: a container that never came back is in no `container ps` filter, so only the recorded-set check sees it."
msgstr "Ta zadnji korak je namerno uporabljen [`sys-ctl-hlth-container` skript](../../../sys-ctl-hlth-container/files/shell/script.sh) Namesto da bi preverili vajo: je tisto, kar opazuje gostitelja v proizvodnji, pozna storitve rojov in odlaga 200 log linije na bolni zabojnik. Navaja se kot skripta, ne kot sistemska enota – enota `OnFailure` začne servis za mehko popravilo in vrtalnik, ki popravi, kar je našel, je prenehal meriti. Tudi vrtalnika ne more nadomestiti. `container ps` filter, tako da ga vidi samo zabeleženo-nastavljeno preverjanje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That makes it easier to see whether the real issue is Docker, journald, a package cache, or project state."
msgstr "Tako je lažje videti, ali je prava številka Docker, dnevnik, predpomnilnik ali država projekta."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That means the bundle is not where logic lives. It is where the architecture becomes a real deployment."
msgstr "To pomeni, da ni tam, kjer živi logika. Tu arhitektura postane prava razporeditev."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That pipe **destroys the exit status**: `make test | tee` reports `tee`'s success even when make ends with `Error 2`. You MUST judge such a run by its `📊 per-target wall-clock` table and its `FAILED TARGETS:` line, never by the exit code."
msgstr "Tista cev. **uniči izhodni status**: `make test | tee` poročila `tee`Uspeh tudi, ko se konča z `Error 2`. Morate soditi tako teči po svojem `📊 per-target wall-clock` tabela in njena `FAILED TARGETS:` Vrstica, nikoli po izhodni kodi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That second step exists because a group grant addresses an Open WebUI group id and ``insert_new_group`` assigns it as a fresh UUID, so the id cannot be known while the env is rendered. The task signs in as the native administrator, resolves or creates the group whose name matches the OIDC claim value, and writes the grant through ``POST /api/v1/configs/tool_servers``. It refuses to act when two groups share a name rather than guessing between them."
msgstr "Ta drugi korak obstaja zato, ker se pomoč skupine nanaša na Open WebUI Identifikator skupine in ``insert_new_group`` ga dodeli kot nov UUID, tako da ID ne more biti znano, medtem ko je env je preveden. Naloga se vpiše kot domači administrator, razreši ali ustvari skupino, katere ime se ujema z vrednostjo zahtevka OIDC, in napiše donacijo prek ``POST /api/v1/configs/tool_servers``. Noče delovati, ko si dve skupini delita ime in ne ugibata."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That second step exists because a group grant addresses an Open WebUI group id and `insert_new_group` assigns it as a fresh UUID, so the id cannot be known while the env is rendered. The task signs in as the native administrator, resolves or creates the group whose name matches the OIDC claim value, and writes the grant through `POST /api/v1/configs/tool_servers`. It refuses to act when two groups share a name rather than guessing between them."
msgstr "Ta drugi korak obstaja zato, ker se pomoč skupine nanaša na Open WebUI Identifikator skupine in `insert_new_group` ga dodeli kot nov UUID, tako da ID ne more biti znano, medtem ko je env je preveden. Naloga se vpiše kot domači administrator, razreši ali ustvari skupino, katere ime se ujema z vrednostjo zahtevka OIDC, in napiše donacijo prek `POST /api/v1/configs/tool_servers`. Noče delovati, ko si dve skupini delita ime in ne ugibata."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "That separation matters:"
msgstr "Ta ločitev je pomembna:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The **Infinito.Nexus Presentation** role automates the setup of an environment using Docker, providing a seamless process for pulling your source repository, building the presentation, and serving the slides through a lightweight HTTP server. It uses **[Reveal.js](https://revealjs.com/)** for building and serving the presentation slides and can be deployed with **Kevin's Package Manager**."
msgstr "– **Infinito.Nexus Presentation** vloga avtomatizira nastavitev okolja z uporabo Dockerja, zagotavlja brezhiben proces za vlečenje izvornega skladišča, gradnjo predstavitve in strežbo diapozitivov skozi lahek strežnik HTTP. Uporablja **[Reveal.js](https://revealjs.com/)** za gradnjo in serviranje predstavitvenih diapozitivov in se lahko uporabljajo z **Kevinov upravitelj paketov**."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The **Infinito.Nexus Presentation** role automates the setup of an environment using Docker, providing a seamless process for pulling your source repository, building the presentation, and serving the slides through a lightweight HTTP server. It uses `Reveal.js <https://revealjs.com/>`__ for building and serving the presentation slides and can be deployed with **Kevin’s Package Manager**."
msgstr "– **Infinito.Nexus Presentation** vloga avtomatizira nastavitev okolja z uporabo Dockerja, zagotavlja brezhiben proces za vlečenje izvornega skladišča, gradnjo predstavitve in strežbo diapozitivov skozi lahek strežnik HTTP. Uporablja `Reveal.js <https://revealjs.com/>`__ za gradnjo in serviranje predstavitvenih diapozitivov in se lahko uporabljajo z **Kevinov upravitelj paketov**."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The **OS-level sandbox** (`sandbox.*` block) is the primary containment. Every Bash command runs inside `bwrap` on Linux or `sandbox-exec` on macOS and is confined by filesystem and network rules. The sandbox itself bounds the blast radius of Bash rather than a per-command allowlist."
msgstr "– **Peskovnik na ravni OS** (`sandbox.*` blok) je primarni zadrževalnik. Vsak ukaz Bash teče noter `bwrap` na Linuxu ali `sandbox-exec` o macOS in je omejen z datotečnim sistemom in pravili omrežja. Peskovnik sam omejuje polmer eksplozije Basha, ne pa seznama dovoljenj po ukazu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The **User Story** MUST follow the \"As a / I want / so that\" format."
msgstr "– **User Zgodba** MORATE slediti \"Kot hočem, tako da\" format."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The **agent receiver (port 8000) IS exposed** (mapped + proxied) for TLS agent registration."
msgstr "– **sprejemnik agentov (pristanišče 8000) IZPOSTAVLJEN** (karted + proksied) za registracijo agenta TLS."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The **exporter** is mandatory: it backs the export (SVG/PDF) and developer handoff features."
msgstr "– **izvoznik** obvezno: podpira izvoz (SVG/PDF) in razvijalec predaja funkcije."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The **only** location outside the repository where transient agent output (downloaded logs, scratch files, intermediate artefacts) MAY be written; see the *Temporary Files* rule in [`AGENTS.md`](../../../../../AGENTS.md)."
msgstr "– **samo** kraj zunaj skladišča, kjer je izhod prehodnega sredstva (prenesene dnevnike, praske, vmesne artefakte) MOGOČE biti zapisana; glej *Začasne datoteke* pravilo v [`AGENTS.md`](../../../../../AGENTS.md)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The **permission lists** (`permissions.{allow,ask,deny}`) are the policy gate that decides whether the agent may attempt a tool call at all. The `allow` list covers non-Bash tools plus the wildcard `Bash(*)`, delegating real gating to `ask` and `deny`. The `deny` list applies as an unconditional hard block. The `ask` list pauses for operator confirmation."
msgstr "– **seznami dovoljenj** (`permissions.{allow,ask,deny}`) so vrata politike, ki se odločijo, ali bo agent sploh poskušal poklicati orodje. – `allow` Seznam zajema orodja, ki niso Bash, in Wildcard `Bash(*)`, prenos pravi gating na `ask` ter `deny`. O `deny` Seznam se uporablja kot brezpogojni trdi blok. – `ask` Seznam premorov za potrditev operatorja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The **sys-ctl-hlth-msmtp** role ensures that your mail transport system stays available by sending a test email at defined intervals. If the email fails, a Telegram alert is triggered, allowing you to detect and address issues before they impact users."
msgstr "– **sys-ctl-hlth-msmtp** vloga zagotavlja, da vaš sistem poštnega prevoza ostane na voljo s pošiljanjem testne e-pošte v določenih intervalih. Če e-pošta ne uspe, se sproži telegramski alarm, ki vam omogoča, da zaznate in obravnavate vprašanja, preden vplivajo na uporabnike."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The **sys-svc-webserver-https** role extends a basic NGINX installation by wiring in everything you need to serve content over HTTPS:"
msgstr "– **sys-svc-webserver-https** vloga širi osnovno NGINX namestitev z ožičenjem v vse, kar potrebujete za služijo vsebine nad HTTPS:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The 2.7.0 image ships 23 tool categories, which are application names (``calendar``, ``files``, ``mail``, ``talk``, …) rather than operations: each bundles its read and its write tools, and the hub offers no setting that removes only the mutating ones. Enabling the ExApp writes ``true`` for every category absent from ``tool_status``, so the hub itself serves all of them, write tools included."
msgstr "– 2.7.0 ladje za slike 23 Kategorije orodja, ki so imena aplikacij (``calendar``, ``files``, ``mail``, ``talk``, ...) namesto operacij: vsak paket sestavlja svoje orodje za branje in pisanje, vozlišče pa ne ponuja nobene nastavitve, ki bi odstranila samo mutirajoče. Omogočanje exApp piše ``true`` za vsako kategorijo, ki je ni ``tool_status``, tako da je vozlišče sam služi vse od njih, vključno z orodjem za pisanje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The 2.7.0 image ships 23 tool categories, which are application names (`calendar`, `files`, `mail`, `talk`, …) rather than operations: each bundles its read and its write tools, and the hub offers no setting that removes only the mutating ones. Enabling the ExApp writes `true` for every category absent from `tool_status`, so the hub itself serves all of them, write tools included."
msgstr "– 2.7.0 ladje za slike 23 Kategorije orodja, ki so imena aplikacij (`calendar`, `files`, `mail`, `talk`, ...) namesto operacij: vsak paket sestavlja svoje orodje za branje in pisanje, vozlišče pa ne ponuja nobene nastavitve, ki bi odstranila samo mutirajoče. Omogočanje exApp piše `true` za vsako kategorijo, ki je ni `tool_status`, tako da je vozlišče sam služi vse od njih, vključno z orodjem za pisanje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The API has no authentication tier: it serves public repository data only, so SSO and logout are disabled and the Playwright persona scenarios are declared blocked for ``biber`` and ``administrator``."
msgstr "– API nima stopnje avtentikacije: služi samo za podatke iz javnega arhiva, zato sta SSO in odjava onemogočena, scenariji Playwright persona pa so razglašeni za blokirane ``biber`` ter ``administrator``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The API has no authentication tier: it serves public repository data only, so SSO and logout are disabled and the Playwright persona scenarios are declared blocked for `biber` and `administrator`."
msgstr "– API nima stopnje avtentikacije: služi samo za podatke iz javnega arhiva, zato sta SSO in odjava onemogočena, scenariji Playwright persona pa so razglašeni za blokirane `biber` ter `administrator`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The AT Protocol PDS, OAuth identity, and the login-broker sidecar pattern. atmo's \"sign in with Bluesky\" points here. The multi-entity `services.yml` (pds/web/view/broker/api) is the template for atmo's appview + worker-runtime split."
msgstr "AT protokol PDS, OAuth identiteto, in vzorec login-broker stranske prikolice. Atmo's \"se prijavite z Bluesky\" Tukaj. Večsubjektov `services.yml` (pds/web/view/broker/api) je predloga za aplikacijo atmosfere + delitev delovnega časa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The AT→AP direction has a clean trigger (firehose) and a clean sink (GraphQL). The reverse direction needs an AT identity to write records as, which is unresolved."
msgstr "Smer AT →AP ima čist sprožilec (Ognjemet) in čisto korito (GrafQL). Obratna smer potrebuje AT identiteto za pisanje zapisov kot, ki je nerešena."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The AUR PKGBUILDs this project consumes carry a checksum on a git source, which makepkg can only reject; integrity rests on the pinned upstream tag fetched over HTTPS."
msgstr "AUR PKGBUILDs ta projekt porabi nosilno kontrolno vsoto na vir git, ki makepkg lahko samo zavrne; integriteta temelji na pripeto priponko nad HTTPS."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The AUR is one origin host with no mirror pool behind it, so a flap there lasts minutes rather than the seconds a pool member needs to rotate out; EXTERNAL_FETCH's ~40s window has been observed losing to a single flap."
msgstr "AUR je eden izvor gostitelj brez ogledala bazen za njim, tako da loputa tam traja nekaj minut, namesto sekund, ki jih mora član bazena vrteti; EXTERNAL_FETCH's ~40so opazili, da je okno izgubilo eno zakrilce."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The Ansible-level `plugins/` directory (filters, lookups, modules) is a different concept from the application-level `addons` topic. See the [plugins README](../../../../../plugins/README.md) for the distinction."
msgstr "Nevidna raven `plugins/` Mapa (filtri, iskalniki, moduli) je drugačen koncept od ravni uporabe `addons` tema. Glejte [vstavki README](../../../../../plugins/README.md) za razliko."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The Argos package index behind LibreTranslate offers 49 languages paired with English. 47 of them are ISO 639-1 codes; `pb` (Brazilian Portuguese) and `zt` (Traditional Chinese) are not and are out of scope. The remaining ISO languages have no model."
msgstr "Za indeksom paketa Argos LibreTranslate ponudbe 49 jeziki v paru z angleščino. 47 od tega so ISO 639-Kaj?1 kode; `pb` (Brazilska portugalščina) ter `zt` (Tradicionalna kitajska) niso in so izven področja uporabe. Preostali jeziki ISO nimajo modela."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The Bash auto-allow path trusts the OS sandbox to confine commands. A missing or broken sandbox backend would cause auto-allow to approve unconfined commands."
msgstr "Bash auto-lough pot zaupa OS peskovnik omejiti ukaze. Manjkajoča ali zlomljena hrbtenica iz peskovnika bi povzročila, da bi samodejno odobrili neurejene ukaze."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The Building Blocks 🧱"
msgstr "Gradbeni bloki 🧱"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CA override that bind-mounts ``CA_TRUST.inject_cert_container`` is emitted under three conditions, and anything that reads the mounted file must ask the same three or it will point at a path that was never mounted. The conditions lived as four hand-copied expressions - both `sys-svc-compose` handlers, `sys-svc-compose-ca/vars/main.yml` and the msmtp template - which is one copy per place that can drift."
msgstr "CA prevlada nad vezanimi zneski ``CA_TRUST.inject_cert_container`` se oddaja pod tremi pogoji, in vse, kar bere pritrjeno datoteko, mora vprašati iste tri ali pa bo pokazal na pot, ki ni bila nikoli nameščena. Pogoji so živeli kot štirje ročno kopirani izrazi - oboje `sys-svc-compose` obdelovalci, `sys-svc-compose-ca/vars/main.yml` in msmtp predlogo - ki je ena kopija na mestu, ki lahko viseče."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CI deploy matrix turns the role catalogue into deploy jobs. Each row is one `role#variant` selection, and each row must state everything that makes its deployment reproducible, because a red job is only useful if an operator can replay exactly it."
msgstr "CI uporablja matrico spremeni katalog vlog v delovna mesta. Vsaka vrstica je ena `role#variant` selekcija, in vsaka vrstica mora navesti vse, kar naredi njeno uvajanje ponovljivo, ker je rdeče delo koristno le, če lahko operater ponovi točno to."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CI gate"
msgstr "Vrata CI"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CI image build is one job per architecture plus a merge job. It does not grow in wall clock, because the architectures build in parallel on their own runners, and each keeps its own build cache tag."
msgstr "Slika CI je eno delo na arhitekturo in združene delo. Ne raste v stenski uri, saj arhitekture gradijo vzporedno na svojih tekačih, in vsak ima svojo gradbeno predpomnilnico."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CI-tested lifecycle envelope, read from ``default.env`` (the SPOT)."
msgstr "Ovojnica življenjskega cikla, testirana s CI, se bere iz ``default.env`` (SPOT)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CI/dev primary domain, read from ``default.env`` (the SPOT)."
msgstr "Primarna domena CI/dev, odčitana iz ``default.env`` (SPOT)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CLI entry point lives at [__main__.py](../../cli/meta/env/__main__.py) under `cli/meta/env/`. Shell consumers source [load.sh](../../scripts/meta/env/load.sh) under `scripts/meta/env/`."
msgstr "Vstopna točka CLI živi na [ main .py](../../cli/meta/env/__main__.py) pod `cli/meta/env/`. Shell potrošniki vir [load.sh](../../scripts/meta/env/load.sh) pod `scripts/meta/env/`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CLI entry point lives at [__main__.py](lint/__main__.py), invoked from [lint.sh](../../scripts/install/lint.sh) as `python3 -m utils.install.lint`. The matching dispatcher [wrapper.sh](../../scripts/install/wrapper.sh) routes `make install-lint` host vs container based on `INFINITO_LINT_RUNNER`."
msgstr "Vstopna točka CLI živi na [ main .py](lint/__main__.py), se sklicuje na [lint.sh](../../scripts/install/lint.sh) kot `python3 -m utils.install.lint`. Ustrezni dispečer [wrapper.sh](../../scripts/install/wrapper.sh) poti `make install-lint` gostitelj vs vsebnik na osnovi `INFINITO_LINT_RUNNER`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CLI entry point lives at ``cli.meta.env`` (`python -m cli.meta.env` or `make dotenv`). It reads the committed ``default.env``, layers runtime context on top (distro, GHA/Act flags, df/meminfo-derived sizes, sha256 secrets, repo owner/name resolution), and writes the resulting ``.env`` to the repo root."
msgstr "Vstopna točka CLI živi na ``cli.meta.env`` (`python -m cli.meta.env` ali `make dotenv`). Bere predane ``default.env``, plasti čas delovanja kontekst na vrhu (distro, zastavice GHA/Act, velikosti df/meminfo, ša256 skrivnosti, lastnik repo / rešitev imena), in piše rezultat ``.env`` do repo korena."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CLI entrypoint lives in `cli/meta/domains/__main__.py`"
msgstr "Vhodna točka CLI živi v `cli/meta/domains/__main__.py`"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CLI keeps the most recent 7 entries (override with `--keep N`) and processes each of the following files:"
msgstr "CLI hrani najnovejše 7 vnosi (razveljavi z `--keep N`) in obdeluje vsako od naslednjih datotek:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CLI prints the planned folder list at init time and the per-round summary at deploy time, so you can confirm the matrix shape before any work happens."
msgstr "CLI natisne načrtovani seznam map ob samem času in povzetek za vsak krog ob času pošiljanja, tako da lahko potrdite matrično obliko pred vsakim delom."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CLI probe sizes its prompt off the smallest declared window, so the model holding that window is the one the request must exclude, and the model that answers instead is what shows the filter ran. `smollm2:135m` is deliberately not the smallest: `8dbdd31b22` measured it running to `n_gen=22011` with context shifts at `n_left=4091`, and a route's `max_tokens` is a default a consumer can override rather than a cap, so it is kept away from the window at which it was seen to run away."
msgstr "Sonda CLI meri svoj poziv od najmanjšega deklariranega okna, zato mora model, ki drži to okno, izključiti, model, ki odgovarja, pa kaže, da je filter tekel. `smollm2:135m` namerno ni najmanjša: `8dbdd31b22` izmeriti teče na `n_gen=22011` s spremembami konteksta na `n_left=4091`, In pot. `max_tokens` je privzeta vrednost, ki jo potrošnik lahko preglasi, ne pa zamaška, zato je odmaknjena od okna, na katerem se je videlo, da beži."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CLI test prints the block it fetched and the output of the replay. The role's own deploy snapshots live in `rescue-diagnostics-<artifact>`."
msgstr "Test CLI natisne blok, ki ga je dobil, in izhod ponovitve. Vlogo lastne uporabe posnetkov v živo `rescue-diagnostics-<artifact>`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CLI under [cli/meta/ci/logs](../../../../cli/meta/ci/logs/README.md) pulls a run's job logs and artefacts in one shot and clusters them by root failure."
msgstr "CLI pod [cli/meta/ci/logs](../../../../cli/meta/ci/logs/README.md) potegne dnevnike in artefakte in jih združi z neuspehom korenin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CLIs default `variant` to `None` so:"
msgstr "Privzeto za CLI `variant` do `None` tako:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CMD-SHELL payload, or the exec argv quoted for a shell."
msgstr "Obremenitev CMD-SHELL ali exec argv, citirana za lupino."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CMD-SHELL spelling of :func:`curl_argv`, quoted for a shell."
msgstr "Črkovanje CMD-SHELL :func:`curl_argv`, citirano za lupino."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CPU architecture is the same kind of property and was not covered at all. Every deploy job ran on `ubuntu-latest`, so every sweep proved amd64 and said nothing about arm64, while the project ships roles whose upstream images, wheels and binaries differ per architecture. A role that cannot run on arm64 was indistinguishable from one nobody had ever tried there."
msgstr "Arhitektura CPU je ista vrsta lastnine in sploh ni bila zajeta. Vsako razporejanje je potekalo naprej `ubuntu-latest`, Vsaka preiskava se je izkazala.64 in ni rekel nič o roki.64, medtem ko so projektne ladje vloge, katerih zgornje slike, kolesa in binarji se razlikujejo po arhitekturi. Vloga, ki ne more delovati na rokah64 je bila nerazločna od tiste, ki je še nihče ni poskusil tam."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The CPU architectures this run spreads its rows over; empty means both."
msgstr "CPU arhitekture ta tek širi svoje vrstice čez; prazno pomeni oboje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The Certbot role provides a ready-to-use, automated solution for SSL/TLS management in your infrastructure. Whether you're managing traditional servers or containerized environments, this role ensures your certificates are always in place and valid."
