msgstr "Obstoječi nalagalnik programov (`utils/cache/applications.py`) MORAJO naložiti vsako `meta/addons/*.yml` Kot druge meta teme. Uveden ni noben nov slovar, ki bi nastal v skladišču."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The expected bill counts the output price, and a long answer can invert the input-price order"
msgstr "Pričakovani račun šteje izhodno ceno, in dolg odgovor lahko obrne vrstni red vhodne cene"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The export-side role enters a play by inventory group membership alone, and ``svc-storage-nfs-server`` ships a variant that runs without it, so the exclusion is gated on that group being populated: without it every volume stays in this role’s capture rather than losing both. Volumes of manager-pinned roles, of roles forcing a non-swarm ``compose_mode_force``, and entries that opt out with ``nfs: false`` stay node-local and stay covered here; compose mode is untouched."
msgstr "Vloga na izvozni strani je v igri samo članstva inventarja in ``svc-storage-nfs-server`` ladje variante, ki teče brez nje, zato je izključitev usmerjena na to skupino, ki je naseljena: brez nje vsaka količina ostane v zavzetju te vloge, namesto da bi izgubila obe. Obseg vlog, vezanih na upravitelja, vlog, ki silijo v netoplo ``compose_mode_force``, in vnosi, ki ne uporabljajo ``nfs: false`` ostanejo vozlišče-lokalno in ostanejo pokriti tukaj; način sestavljanja je nedotaknjen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The export-side role enters a play by inventory group membership alone, and `svc-storage-nfs-server` ships a variant that runs without it, so the exclusion is gated on that group being populated: without it every volume stays in this role's capture rather than losing both. Volumes of manager-pinned roles, of roles forcing a non-swarm `compose_mode_force`, and entries that opt out with `nfs: false` stay node-local and stay covered here; compose mode is untouched."
msgstr "Vloga na izvozni strani je v igri samo članstva inventarja in `svc-storage-nfs-server` Ladje varianto, ki teče brez nje, tako da je izključitev vrata na tej skupini, ki se naseljuje: brez tega vsaka količina ostane v zajemu te vloge, namesto da bi izgubili obe. Obseg vlog, vezanih na upravitelja, vlog, ki silijo v netoplo `compose_mode_force`, in vnosi, ki ne uporabljajo `nfs: false` ostanejo vozlišče-lokalno in ostanejo pokriti tukaj; način sestavljanja je nedotaknjen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The external addon test MUST emit warnings, not failures, when a monitored addon has a newer upstream version."
msgstr "Preskus zunanjega dodatka MORA oddajati opozorila, ne napak, če ima spremljani dodatek novejšo različico v zgornjem toku."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The external addon test MUST emit warnings, not failures, when a supported catalog adapter detects a new relevant addon that is not listed in `meta/addons/`."
msgstr "Preskus zunanjega dodatka MORA oddajati opozorila, ne napak, ko podprt katalogski adapter zazna nov ustrezni addon, ki ni naveden v `meta/addons/`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The extraction and the translation client share this one function, so a message the catalogs withhold is the same message the client would have refused to send."
msgstr "Izvleček in prevajalski odjemalec delita to funkcijo, zato je sporočilo, ki ga katalogi zadržijo, isto sporočilo, ki bi ga stranka zavrnila."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The fact is not merely late, it is wrong while it is late. Facts are read before the daemon config is applied, so ``docker0`` still carries docker's own default; writing the pools then moves the bridge underneath it. A swarm node measured ``172.17.0.1`` in daemon.json against a live ``10.208.0.1``, which is why the declaration answers here and the fact never does."
msgstr "Dejstvo ni le pozno, ampak tudi napačno, medtem ko je pozno. Dejstva se berejo pred uporabo demonskega konfiga. ``docker0`` Še vedno nosi privzeti privzeti pas; pisanje bazenov nato premakne most pod njim. Izmerjeno rojsko vozlišče ``172.17.0.1`` v daemon.json proti živemu ``10.208.0.1``, zato izjava odgovarja tukaj in dejstvo nikoli ne."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The factors are `locality`, `cost`, `speed`, `caching` and `throughput`. `cost` is the expected bill for this request, input price times estimated input tokens plus output price times requested output, because ranking on the input price alone reads the cheaper half: an output token commonly costs several times an input one, and a short prompt with a long answer inverts the order the input price suggests. `caching` prefers a route that can reuse a cached prefix, which is the largest real saving for an agent with a stable system prompt. `throughput` reads the catalogued `tpm`, the only quota the catalog carries."
msgstr "Dejavniki so: `locality`, `cost`, `speed`, `caching` ter `throughput`. `cost` je pričakovani račun za to zahtevo, vhodne cene krat ocenjeni vhodni žetoni plus izhodne cene časi zahtevana proizvodnja, ker razvrstitev na vhodno ceno samo prebere cenejšo polovico: izhodni žeton pogosto stane večkrat vhodni ena, in kratek odgovor z dolgim odgovorom obrne vrstni red vhodni ceni predlaga. `caching` ima raje pot, ki lahko ponovno uporabi predpono, ki je največji pravi prihranek za sredstvo s stabilnim sistemom. `throughput` bere katalogizirano `tpm`, Edina kvota, ki jo ima katalog."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The fallback Jinja string in the base `meta/services.yml` is the safety net for the case where neither variant overrides the flag and the operator still adds `web-app-discourse` to the inventory groups manually: the runtime `lookup('config', application_id, 'services.discourse.enabled')` then renders the conditional against the real `group_names` and the wp-discourse plugin install enables itself accordingly."
msgstr "Rezervna Jinja struna v bazi `meta/services.yml` je varnostna mreža za primer, ko nobena od variant ne prevlada nad zastavo in operater še vedno dodaja `web-app-discourse` za skupine inventarja ročno: čas delovanja `lookup('config', application_id, 'services.discourse.enabled')` potem pogojno proti resničnemu `group_names` in wp-discourse plugin namestitev omogoča sama ustrezno."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The fallback is not a default -- the value still comes from the single source, just read directly instead of through a generated ``.env``. It is what lets a CLI run outside ``scripts/meta/env/load.sh`` without either inventing a value or dying on a key the repository does declare."
msgstr "Rezerva ni privzeta -- vrednost še vedno prihaja iz enega vira, samo berite neposredno namesto skozi ustvarjeno ``.env``. To je tisto, kar CLI teče ven ``scripts/meta/env/load.sh`` brez izuma vrednosti ali umiranja na ključu, ki ga repozitorij prijavi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The field names on the provider record are only discoverable by unpacking the purchased artifact, so step 3 has to be measured against the extension actually installed rather than assumed from this note."
msgstr "Imena polj na evidenci ponudnika so odkrita samo z razpakiranjem kupljenega artefakta, zato korak 3 je treba meriti glede na dejansko nameščeno razširitev, ne pa predvidevati iz te opombe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The file MUST live at `roles/<application_id>/meta/variants.yml`."
msgstr "Datoteka MORA živeti na `roles/<application_id>/meta/variants.yml`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The file is a mapping of logical package id to a distro mapping. Keys are ``ansible_facts['os_family']`` values; a lowercase distribution name (``ubuntu``, ``centos``, ``fedora``, ``arch``, ``debian``) overrides its family when that one distribution differs::"
msgstr "Datoteka je kartiranje logičnega paketa ID na distro kartiranje. Ključi so ``ansible_facts['os_family']`` vrednosti; ime manjše distribucije (``ubuntu``, ``centos``, ``fedora``, ``arch``, ``debian``) prevlada nad svojo družino, kadar se ta razdelitev razlikuje:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The file is edited line by line rather than parsed and re-dumped: these files carry ``# nocheck:`` directives and hand-tuned ordering that a YAML round-trip would drop."
msgstr "Datoteka je urejena po vrsti in ne razčlenjena in ponovno ustavljena: te datoteke nosijo ``# nocheck:`` Navodila in ročno uglašeno naročilo, da bo YaML povratna pot padla."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The file is not optional. It lives beside ``roles/``, which the packaging config excludes from the wheel just as it excludes ``meta/``, so any context that can resolve a role name also carries this file. A missing file is a broken checkout and raises rather than degrading to an empty category tree, which would silently strip every category prefix off every role name."
msgstr "Datoteka ni neobvezna. Živi poleg. ``roles/``, ki ga pakiranje konfig izključuje iz kolesa, tako kot izključuje ``meta/``, tako da vsak kontekst, ki lahko razreši ime vloge nosi tudi to datoteko. Manjkajoča datoteka je lomljena odjava in se ne ponižuje na prazno drevo kategorije, ki bi tiho odstranilo vsako predpono kategorije z vsakega imena vloge."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The file root IS the services map (no ``services.`` wrapper), so the walker tracks one nesting level: top-level service keys and their immediate ``version:`` field."
msgstr "Koren datoteke je zemljevid storitev (ni ``services.`` ovoj), tako sprehajalec sledi eno stopnjo gnezdenja: top-level servisne tipke in njihov takojšnji ``version:`` Polje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The file root of ``meta/services.yml`` IS the services map; there is no ``services.`` wrapper to walk into."
msgstr "Koren datoteke ``meta/services.yml`` IS zemljevid storitev; ne obstaja ``services.`` Ovitek za vstop."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, no-python-format
msgid "The file's pre-``%changelog`` head is preserved verbatim. The ``%changelog`` section is replaced with one stanza per entry plus the trailing notice. Returns ``True`` when the file was rewritten, ``False`` when nothing happened (missing file, no ``%changelog`` section, no entries, or dry run)."
msgstr "Datoteka je pred-``%changelog`` glava je ohranjena dobesedno. – ``%changelog`` oddelek se nadomesti z enim kilom na vnos in obvestilom. Vračila ``True`` ko je bila datoteka ponovno napisana, ``False`` ko se ni nič zgodilo (manjkajoča datoteka, št. ``%changelog`` oddelek, ni vnosov ali suhi tek)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The files here are **not application-specific**. They are **infrastructure helpers** used by other roles, health checks, CI jobs, and runtime scripts that interact with Docker containers in a controlled and reproducible way."
msgstr "Datoteke so tukaj. **nespecifično za uporabo**Saj so. **Pomočniki infrastrukture** ki jih uporabljajo druge vloge, zdravstveni pregledi, delovna mesta CI in scenariji časa delovanja, ki nadzorovano in ponovljivo komunicirajo z zabojniki Docker."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The filesystem is a preference unless a human names it 🗄️"
msgstr "Datotečni sistem je prednost, če ga človek ne imenuje 🗄️"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The filesystem is the one axis a token built here leaves out. The title states the kind the matrix *assigned*, which a deploy is allowed to fall back from when the host cannot serve it, so the title does not prove what the job ran on. Writing it into a token would also state it as named by a human, which makes it binding (:func:`utils.github.variant.axes.assign`): a retrigger would then fail on the very condition the fallback exists to absorb. The retrigger lets the rotation assign it again and reports what it got. Reading the tokens out of a finished run is what lets a retrigger replay exactly what failed and start the regular line where that run stopped, instead of aggregating to role ids and guessing the rest."
msgstr "Datotečni sistem je edina os, ki jo tukaj izdelujejo. Naslov navaja vrsto matrice *dodeljena*, ki se lahko razporedi nazaj, ko gostitelj ne more služiti, tako da naslov ne dokazuje, kaj je delo tekel naprej. Če bi jo napisali v žeton, bi jo imenovali tudi človek. (:func:`utils.github.variant.axes.assign`): retrigger bi potem ne pod pogojem, da je rezervni obstaja absorbirati. Retrigger pusti rotacijo ponovno dodeliti in poroča, kaj je dobil. Branje žetonov iz končanega teka je tisto, kar omogoča retrigger ponovno predvajati točno tisto, kar je spodletelo in začeti redno linijo, kjer je ta tek ustavil, namesto da bi združevanje za vlogo ids in ugibanje ostalo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The final `done` job aggregates all deploy, install, and development gates. CI is considered green only when this job succeeds."
msgstr "Final `done` Zaposlitev združuje vse razporeditve, namestitev in razvoj. CI velja za zeleno šele, ko to delo uspe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The first usable address, e.g. ``192.168.24.1``."
msgstr "Prvi uporabni naslov, npr. ``192.168.24.1``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The fix is to **externalise the engines** into central, pinned `svc-db-*` / `svc-dns-*` roles (exactly like `svc-db-postgres` / `svc-db-mariadb`) and have apps connect to them. Apps then own only user-data volumes (NFS-safe) and need no pin."
msgstr "Popraviti je na **eksternalizirati motorje** v sredino, pripeta `svc-db-*` / `svc-dns-*` Vloge (Točno tako. `svc-db-postgres` / `svc-db-mariadb`) in imajo aplikacije povezati z njimi. Aplikacije imajo v lasti samo uporabniške podatke (Varnost NFS) In ne potrebujem igle."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The fix loop and its forbidden shortcuts are the `test-fix` skill's; this skill only pins the command and how to read its result."
msgstr "Fiksna zanka in njene prepovedane bližnjice so `test-fix` spretnost je; ta spretnost samo zapiči ukaz in kako prebrati svoj rezultat."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The flag is mandatory, enforced by [test_onion_port_flag.py](../../../../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_onion_port_flag.py): every category declared under `local` or `public` needs a `true` or a `false`, and every `false` needs `# nocheck: onion-flag` plus the reason it is false. Four groups are settled centrally instead and take no flag: the categories a hidden service cannot carry (`relay`, `media`, `stun_turn`, `stun_turn_tls`), the proxy-fronted `http`, `sso` and `websocket`, the implicit-TLS variants (`smtps`, `imaps`, `pop3s`, `ldaps`), and any entity that already answers the question through `exposed:`."
msgstr "Zastava je obvezna in jo je treba uveljaviti [test_onion_port_flag.py](../../../../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_onion_port_flag.py): vsaka kategorija, prijavljena pod `local` ali `public` a `true` ali a `false`, in vsak `false` potrebe `# nocheck: onion-flag` Pa še razlog je lažen. Štiri skupine se poravnajo centralno in ne prevzamejo zastave: kategorije skrite storitve ne morejo nositi (`relay`, `media`, `stun_turn`, `stun_turn_tls`), pooblaščeni `http`, `sso` ter `websocket`, implicitne različice TLS (`smtps`, `imaps`, `pop3s`, `ldaps`), in vsak subjekt, ki že odgovarja na vprašanje skozi `exposed:`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The flavor enum is ``{oidc, oauth2, saml}`` with ``oidc`` as the default when omitted. The ``is_proxy_gated`` predicate is the one place that encodes \"the oauth2-proxy sidecar fronts this role\" — every other layer MUST consult this helper instead of re-implementing the ``enabled AND flavor == 'oauth2'`` compound. The ``oauth2_*`` keys expose the gated upstream config so call sites resolve cross-role data through one named property rather than a literal ``lookup('config', app_id, 'services.sso.oauth2.<sub>')`` (which would otherwise trip the literal-protocol-lookup and lookup-config-path static-scan guards)."
msgstr "Okus enum je ``{oidc, oauth2, saml}`` z ``oidc`` kot privzeto, če je izpuščeno. – ``is_proxy_gated`` Predikat je edini kraj, ki kodira \"oauth2-proxy sidecart predstavlja to vlogo\" — se mora vsaka druga plast posvetovati s tem pomočnikom, namesto da ponovno izvaja ``enabled AND flavor == 'oauth2'`` Sestavina. – ``oauth2_*`` tipke razkrijejo dostopno gornjo config, tako da klicne strani rešujejo podatke o navzkrižni roli preko ene imenovane lastnine in ne dobesedne ``lookup('config', app_id, 'services.sso.oauth2.<sub>')`` (ki bi drugače spotaknili dobesedno-protokol-ogled in iskati-config-pot statično-kan stražarji)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The fleet is deployed on **every** cluster node, but not as a ``docker stack`` service (``workload: node-local`` in ``meta/services.yml``): each runner needs the docker socket and the registered identity of exactly its node. The image is built once on the manager and distributed through the registry dependency (``svc-registry-docker``), the only part that runs as a swarm service."
msgstr "Flota je razporejena **vsak** grozdno vozlišče, vendar ne kot ``docker stack`` storitev (``workload: node-local`` v ``meta/services.yml``): vsak tekač potrebuje docker vtičnico in registrirano identiteto točno svoje vozlišče. Slika je enkrat zgrajena na upravitelju in razdeljena z odvisnostjo od registra (``svc-registry-docker``), edini del, ki deluje kot roj storitev."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The fleet is deployed on **every** cluster node, but not as a `docker stack` service (`workload: node-local` in `meta/services.yml`): each runner needs the docker socket and the registered identity of exactly its node. The image is built once on the manager and distributed through the registry dependency (`svc-registry-docker`), the only part that runs as a swarm service."
msgstr "Flota je razporejena **vsak** grozdno vozlišče, vendar ne kot `docker stack` storitev (`workload: node-local` v `meta/services.yml`): vsak tekač potrebuje docker vtičnico in registrirano identiteto točno svoje vozlišče. Slika je enkrat zgrajena na upravitelju in razdeljena z odvisnostjo od registra (`svc-registry-docker`), edini del, ki deluje kot roj storitev."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The floor keeps a short entry out: ``Situation`` becomes ``Lage`` and loses half its characters while saying the same thing. A passage past it that comes back halved has dropped a clause."
msgstr "Tla imajo kratek vnos. ``Situation`` postane ``Lage`` in izgubi polovico likov, medtem ko govori isto. Prehod mimo njega, ki se je vrnil na pol, je izpustil klavzulo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The focus here is not feature work, but control and safety: development workflows sometimes need a softer security posture, while cleanup paths must leave the system in a predictable state again. That makes this area less about convenience and more about trust, reversibility, and clear operational boundaries. 🔒"
msgstr "Poudarek tukaj ni funkcija delo, vendar nadzor in varnost: razvoj poteka dela včasih potrebujejo mehkejšo varnostno držo, medtem ko čiščenje poti mora pustiti sistem v predvidljivem stanju znova. Zaradi tega je na tem področju manj udobja in več zaupanja, reverzibilnosti in jasnih operativnih meja. 🔒"

