# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The lint test in ``tests/lint/repository/settings/test_claude_sorted.py`` requires every hand-curated array to stay ASCII-sorted ascending so diffs stay reviewable and merge conflicts stay minimal. Tools that auto-extend the file (e.g. permission auto-allowlists) tend to append unsorted; this script puts everything back in order."
msgstr "Preskus line v ``tests/lint/repository/settings/test_claude_sorted.py`` zahteva, da vsi ročno sušeni nizi ostanejo ASCII-sortirani naraščajoči, tako da diffs ostanejo pregledani in združijo konflikte ostanejo minimalni. Orodja, ki samodejno razširijo datoteko (Npr. avtodopustni seznami) nagibajo, da dodate nesortiran; ta scenarij postavlja vse nazaj v red."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The lint test that fails when a requirement file is fully checked off ([tests/lint/repository/documentation/test_requirements_completeness.py](../../../tests/lint/repository/documentation/test_requirements_completeness.py)) still lives here. It now imports the archive primitives from `pkgmgr.actions.archive`, pulled in via the `dev` extra in [pyproject.toml](../../../pyproject.toml)."
msgstr "Preskus line, ki ne uspe, ko je datoteka z zahtevami v celoti odkljukana ([tests/lint/repository/documentation/test_requirements_completeness.py](../../../tests/lint/repository/documentation/test_requirements_completeness.py)) Še vedno živi tukaj. Zdaj uvaža arhiv primitivcev iz `pkgmgr.actions.archive`, potegnil skozi `dev` ekstra [pyproject.toml](../../../pyproject.toml)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The list below was produced by grepping each `roles/<role>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js` for `biber|BIBER`. A role appears under \"missing\" iff it has a Playwright spec, no biber references, AND its policy classification (next column) says one is expected. Each checkbox MUST be closed by reading the spec end to end, deciding whether the role is in scope, and then either adding the biber scenario (and the env keys) OR documenting in the commit message why the role is exempt and removing it from this list."
msgstr "Spodnji seznam je bil izdelan tako, da se je vsak narisal. `roles/<role>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js` besedilo `biber|BIBER`. Vloga se pojavi pod \"missing\" če ima specifikacijo Playwright, brez biber reference, in njegovo klasifikacijo politike (naslednji stolpec) Pravi, da se pričakuje. Vsako potrditveno polje MORA biti zaprto z branjem specifikacije konca do konca, odločanjem o tem, ali je vloga na področju uporabe, in nato dodajanje scenarija biber (in env tipke) ALI dokumentiranje sporočila o zavezi, zakaj je vloga izvzeta, in njegovo črtanje s tega seznama."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The list below was produced by grepping each role's `meta/services.yml` for an `ldap` block with `enabled` set to something other than `false`. Each checkbox MUST be closed by reading the spec end to end, deciding whether the role exposes a test-drivable LDAP auth surface, and then either adding the LDAP scenario OR documenting in the commit message why the role is exempt (e.g. the LDAP integration is consumer-side only, with no Playwright- reachable login UI)."
msgstr "Spodnji seznam je bil izdelan tako, da je vsako vlogo zapolnil. `meta/services.yml` za `ldap` blok z `enabled` nastavljeno na nekaj drugega kot `false`. Vsako potrditveno polje MORA biti zaprto z branjem spec konec do konca, odločanje o tem, ali vloga izpostavlja testno-pogonsko LDAP auth površino, in nato bodisi dodajanje LDAP scenarij ALI dokumentiranje v sporočilu za prijavo, zakaj je vloga izvzeta (npr. integracija LDAP je samo na strani potrošnikov, brez uporabniškega vmesnika Playwright)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The list is cut into serial chunks with a hard boundary at the priority/regular seam (:mod:`cli.meta.ci.chunks`), sized by the run's job and queue budget (:mod:`cli.meta.ci.slots`)."
msgstr "Seznam je razrezan na serijske delce s trdo mejo na prednostni/redni šivi (:mod:`cli.meta.ci.chunks`), po velikosti glede na delovno mesto in proračun v vrsti (:mod:`cli.meta.ci.slots`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The list was held against the repository by three lints that parsed this section. They are gone, and the trade is deliberate: a lint that reads prose ties every role addition to an edit here, and the audit is a review record rather than a runtime registry. What they proved while they ran is worth keeping: the classification check named twenty-four roles whose audit entry contradicted their own metadata the first time it ran, nine of them shipping an adapter while the list still called them untried candidates. Without them, a role added later is absent here until someone notices."
msgstr "Seznam so proti skladišču hranili trije listi, ki so razčlenili ta del. Ni jih več in trgovina je premišljena: lin, ki bere prozo, povezuje vsak dodatek k urejanju tukaj, revizija pa je recenzijski zapis in ne register časa delovanja. Kar so dokazali med tekom, je vredno obdržati: klasifikacijski pregled je imenoval štiriindvajset vlog, katerih revizijski vnos je bil v nasprotju z njihovimi lastnimi metapodatki, ko je prvič tekel, devet jih je poslalo adapter, medtem ko jih je seznam še vedno imenoval neizkušene kandidate. Brez njih je vloga, dodana kasneje, odsotna, dokler kdo ne opazi."

