# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Trusted fork PRs 🔓"
msgstr "Zaupne vilice PR 🔓"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Trusted fork PRs: a maintainer-applied *trusted-pr* label runs a fork PR as deliberately released code — the orchestrator skips the fork-prerequisite wait and the privileged *pull_request_target* build switches its source from the base merge ref to the raw PR head, while the built image keeps the merge-SHA tag so every downstream consumer is unchanged. The label is the only switch (applying a label is collaborator-only on GitHub, so fork authors cannot grant it), build-orchestration scripts always come from the base repository, and both unlabeled fork PRs and same-repository PRs are untouched. See [the fork-PR pipeline](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pipeline.md) and [the contributor fork workflow](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pull-request.md)."
msgstr "Zaupne vilice PR: vzdrževalec uporablja *zaupanja vreden-pr* Zaloga vodi vilice PR kot namerno sproščeno kodo – orkestrator preskoči vilice-predpogoj čakanja in privilegiran *pull_request_target* Gradnja preklopi svoj vir iz baze spajanje ref v surovo PR glavo, medtem ko zgrajena slika ohranja spajanje-SHA oznako, tako da je vsak nadaljnji potrošnik nespremenjen. Oznaka je edino stikalo (uporaba nalepke je samo sodelavka na GitHubu, zato je avtorji vilic ne morejo podeliti), build-orchestration skripte vedno prihajajo iz baznega skladišča, in tako neoznačene vilice PR in isto-repitory PR so nedotaknjeni. Glej. [cevovod vilice-PR](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pipeline.md) ter [delovni tok vilic, ki prispevajo](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pull-request.md)."

