# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When the log carries the matrix-deploy round/pass markers, the result is segmented (one block of records per variant round + pass). Otherwise a single combined block is returned. Runtime rows are read from the ``ROLES RECAP`` sections only (never ``TASKS RECAP``, whose role-less task rows would double-count); a log without any recap header falls back to reading every profile-shaped line. The recap ``total`` line survives as the ``total`` row so consumers can cross-check the parsed sum. Per-host task results (``ok:``, ``changed:``, ``skipping:``, ``fatal:``, ``failed:`` under a ``TASK [role : ...]`` header) accumulate into each record's ``hosts`` field; delegation targets (``[host -> other]``) count for the source host. Raises FileNotFoundError when the log is absent (the caller turns that into a hard failure)."
msgstr "Ko log nosi matrično-razporejene okrogle/pasovne oznake, je rezultat razčlenjen (en blok zapisov na variantni krog + prehod). V nasprotnem primeru se vrne en združeni blok. Vrstice poteka se berejo iz ``ROLES RECAP`` samo profili (Nikoli ``TASKS RECAP``, katerih opravilne vrstice brez vloge bi se dvojno štele); dnevnik brez recap glave pade nazaj na branje vseh profilnih vrstic. Pokrovček ``total`` Linija preživi kot ``total`` vrstica, da lahko potrošniki navzkrižno preverijo razčlenjeno vsoto. Rezultati opravil na gostitelja (``ok:``, ``changed:``, ``skipping:``, ``fatal:``, ``failed:`` pod a ``TASK [role : ...]`` glava) kopičijo v vsakem zapisu ``hosts`` področje; cilji prenosa (``[host -> other]``) Štej za izvornega gostitelja. Dvigne datotekoNotFoundError, ko dnevnik ni na voljo (klicatelj to spremeni v težko napako.)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When the oauth2-proxy SSO flavor is active, Snipe-IT’s native ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` is enabled via the ``Setting`` model (``login_remote_user_enabled``, ``login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME``). nginx gates ``/login`` through oauth2-proxy/Keycloak and injects the verified ``X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`` header, which Snipe-IT matches against ``users.username`` (the user must pre-exist and be activated — sync them via LDAP) to mint a native ``snipeit_session``. Visitors without a matching activated user silently fall through to the normal login form (no error). The password/LDAP login form stays available as a fallback (``login_common_disabled = 0``), and the in-app logout is redirected to the central OIDC end-session URL."
msgstr "Ko oauth2-proxy SSO okus je aktiven, Snipe-IT je domačin ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` omogočen preko ``Setting`` model (``login_remote_user_enabled``, ``login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME``). ginx vrata ``/login`` skozi oauth2proksi/Keycloak in injicira preverjeno ``X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`` glava, ki se ujema s Snipe-IT ``users.username`` (uporabnik mora vnaprej obstajati in biti aktiviran – sinhronizirati jih mora prek LDAP) za kovanje domačina ``snipeit_session``. Obiskovalci brez ujemajočega se aktiviranega uporabnika tiho padejo na običajen prijavni obrazec (brez napake). Geslo / LDAP prijavni obrazec ostane na voljo kot rezervni (``login_common_disabled = 0``), in odjava v aplikaciji je preusmerjena na osrednji končni URL OIDC."

