# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] Database-backed integrations use per-application views/collections/indexes and read-only principals; no test or configuration contains a shared engine administrator credential. One database-backed surface is enabled, Qdrant, and auditing it found the engine running with no authentication at all: its environment set the HTTP port and disabled telemetry and nothing else, so every container that reached its network held full read, write and delete access to every collection, and the surface's read-only promise rested entirely on the adapter's own contract naming only GET routes. Qdrant 1.19 offers what was needed: `read_only_api_key` forces authentication on every request and grants reads only. The engine now declares both keys, the adapter presents the read-only one through `api-key`, and the full key goes only to consumers that own data here, which is asserted by a unit test on the resolver because handing the read-only key out anywhere else would make it meaningless. A contract that named a write route is now refused by the engine rather than only by the adapter. Two limits stay, and neither is a credential problem: Qdrant has no per-consumer principals, only engine-wide keys, so \"read-only principal\" is as narrow as this engine goes without JWT RBAC; and `qdrant_list_collections` enumerates the whole engine, which is bounded today by there being one data owner but is not a per-application view. The path parameter of `qdrant_get_collection` is not a traversal risk: the adapter percent-encodes it with an empty safe set, so a `../` argument reaches Qdrant as a literal collection name."
msgstr "[x] Integracije, podprte z zbirko podatkov, se uporabljajo na aplikacijo views/collections/indexes in samo za branje glavnice; noben preskus ali konfiguracija ne vsebuje skupnega administratorja motorja. Omogočena je ena stran baze podatkov. Qdrant, in revidiranje je našel motor, ki deluje brez overovitve sploh: njegovo okolje je nastavilo HTTP vrata in onemogočeno telemetrijo in nič drugega, tako da je vsak zabojnik, ki je dosegel svoje omrežje potekala v celoti brati, pisati in izbrisati dostop do vsake zbirke, in površina je samo bralno obljubo v celoti počivala na lastni pogodbi adapter je poimenovanje le poti GET. Qdrant 1.19 ponuja, kar je bilo potrebno: `read_only_api_key` prisili k avtentikaciji na vsaki zahtevi in donaciji, ki se bere samo. Motor zdaj razglasi oba ključa, adapter predstavlja samo branje skozi `api-key`, in celoten ključ gre samo za potrošnike, ki imajo tukaj lastne podatke, kar se uveljavlja s preskusom enote na reševalcu, ker bi bila izdaja ključa samo za branje kjerkoli drugje nesmiselna. Pogodbo, ki je poimenovala pot pisanja, zdaj motor raje zavrne kot pa samo adapter. Dve meji ostajata, prav tako pa tudi ni težava v zaupanju: Qdrant nima glavnice na potrošnika, samo ključe za vse motorje. \"glavnica samo za branje\" je tako ozek, kot gre ta motor brez JWT RBAC; in `qdrant_list_collections` Našteva celoten motor, ki je danes omejen z enim lastnikom podatkov, vendar ni prikaz na uporabo. Parameter poti `qdrant_get_collection` ni traverzalno tveganje: adapter odstotek ga kodira s prazno sef, tako da `../` argument doseže Qdrant kot dobesedno ime zbirke."

