msgid "```svc-ai-litellm`` <../svc-ai-litellm/>`__ publishes one routing alias. When this service is deployed, the gateway’s pre-call hook asks it which of the eligible models should answer, passing the prompt as the state and the surviving aliases as the options of a single ``choice`` question. ``services.litellm.router.strategy`` follows ``services.s1.enabled``, so deploying this role is what switches the gateway from a weighted score to a System One decision."
msgstr "```svc-ai-litellm`` <../svc-ai-litellm/>`__ publishes one routing alias. When this service is deployed, the gateway’s pre-call hook asks it which of the eligible models should answer, passing the prompt as the state and the surviving aliases as the options of a single ``choice`` question. ``services.litellm.router.strategy`` follows ``services.s1.enabled``, tako uvajanje te vloge je tisto, kar preklopi prehod od tehtanega rezultat na System One odločitev."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/01_admin.yml`` <./tasks/01_admin.yml>`__ provisions only the administrator in Shopware’s user table. ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``services.sso.flavor: oidc``, so no oauth2-proxy fronts the role and the storefront carries no authenticated surface at all; the Keycloak login provider that ```tasks/setup/oidc.yml`` <./tasks/setup/oidc.yml>`__ configures covers the administration backend alone. ``biber`` therefore has no account in any matrix variant and ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` unconditionally."
msgstr "```tasks/01_admin.yml`` <./tasks/01_admin.yml>`__ provisions only the administrator in Shopware’s user table. ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``services.sso.flavor: oidc``, so no oauth2-proxy fronts the role and the storefront carries no authenticated surface at all; the Keycloak login provider that ```tasks/setup/oidc.yml`` <./tasks/setup/oidc.yml>`__ configures covers the administration backend alone. ``biber`` therefore has no account in any matrix variant and ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` Brezpogojno."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/01_setup.yml`` <./tasks/01_setup.yml>`__ seeds only the administrator into Magento’s admin table (``bin/magento setup:install --admin-user``, credentials from ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); ``biber`` reaches the backend solely through the oauth2-proxy declared in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that proxy is absent and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` and runs in every variant."
msgstr "```tasks/01_setup.yml`` <./tasks/01_setup.yml>`__ seeds only the administrator into Magento’s admin table (``bin/magento setup:install --admin-user``, credentials from ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); ``biber`` reaches the backend solely through the oauth2-proxy declared in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that proxy is absent and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` in teče v vsaki varianti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/05_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/05_administrator.yml>`__ creates the account with ``tootctl accounts create`` and never sets or captures a password, so ``ADMIN_PASSWORD`` — the Keycloak secret — cannot drive Mastodon’s native ``/auth/sign_in``; ``biber`` has no Mastodon account at all, since the OIDC sign-in (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The SeaweedFS companion scenario (```files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`` <./files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js>`__) drives the same admin journey and skips on the same flag."
msgstr "```tasks/05_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/05_administrator.yml>`__ creates the account with ``tootctl accounts create`` and never sets or captures a password, so ``ADMIN_PASSWORD`` — the Keycloak secret — cannot drive Mastodon’s native ``/auth/sign_in``; ``biber`` has no Mastodon account at all, since the OIDC sign-in (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The SeaweedFS companion scenario (```files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`` <./files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js>` ) vozi isto potovanje admin in preskoči na isto zastavo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml`` <tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml>`__ runs after ``update.php``. It includes the shared gateway consumer contract, then reads both globals back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` and asserts the provider, the base URL and the model, so an unconfigured surface cannot reach a green deploy."
msgstr "```tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml`` <tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml>`__ runs after ``update.php``. It includes the shared gateway consumer contract, then reads both globals back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` in uveljavlja ponudnika, osnovni URL in model, tako da nenastavljena površina ne more doseči zelene uporabe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates a dedicated non-superuser owner (``mcp@<canonical-domain>``, unusable password) plus its own workspace, and binds the endpoint to that pair."
msgstr "```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates a dedicated non-superuser owner (``mcp@<canonical-domain>``, neuporabno geslo) In svoj delovni prostor, in veže končno točko na ta par."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```templates/config.exs.j2`` <./templates/config.exs.j2>`__ wires Keycloak as the only login provider this role configures, and ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ creates no Mobilizon account; ``MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_DISABLE_DATABASE_LOGIN`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) additionally closes the database login whenever LDAP is on. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants neither persona has credentials, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona and the baseline assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "```templates/config.exs.j2`` <./templates/config.exs.j2>`__ wires Keycloak as the only login provider this role configures, and ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ creates no Mobilizon account; ``MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_DISABLE_DATABASE_LOGIN`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) additionally closes the database login whenever LDAP is on. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants neither persona has credentials, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona in osnovne trditve potekajo brezpogojno."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ seeds only the administrator into SuiteCRM (``SUITECRM_ADMIN_USERNAME`` / ``SUITECRM_ADMIN_PASSWORD``); ``biber`` reaches the app through SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak, where ``SAML_AUTO_CREATE`` mints the account on first assertion. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants there is no SAML entry point and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` for the generic persona journeys (the LDAP spec still signs ``biber`` in from the directory). The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` and runs in every variant."
msgstr "```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ seeds only the administrator into SuiteCRM (``SUITECRM_ADMIN_USERNAME`` / ``SUITECRM_ADMIN_PASSWORD``); ``biber`` reaches the app through SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak, where ``SAML_AUTO_CREATE`` mints the account on first assertion. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants there is no SAML entry point and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` for the generic persona journeys (the LDAP spec still signs ``biber`` in from the directory). The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` in teče v vsaki varianti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` in every matrix variant, because the shared persona helper cannot drive this role’s sign-in in any of them. Three independent reasons, each sufficient on its own:"
msgstr "```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` v vsaki matrični varianti, ker skupni persona pomočnik ne more poganjati prijave te vloge v nobenem od njih. Trije neodvisni razlogi, vsak zase zadostni:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``adapter``:         immutable source contract of a repository-owned adapter. ``category_allowlist`` suits an upstream that switches whole categories and offers no per-tool filter, where a tool allowlist would be unenforceable; ``mcp_passthrough`` fronts an upstream that already speaks MCP instead of translating REST. ``upstream_path`` names that upstream where it lives on the application's own vhost, so the proxy can hide it: reaching it directly walks past the allowlist the adapter exists to enforce. A provider whose upstream is a separate sidecar declares ``upstream_network`` instead and has nothing to hide there."
msgstr "``adapter``: nespremenljiva izvorna pogodba adapterja v lasti skladišča. ``category_allowlist`` ustreza gornjemu toku, ki preklaplja cele kategorije in ne ponuja filtra na orodje, kjer bi bil seznam orodij neizvršljiv; ``mcp_passthrough`` Spredaj zgoraj, ki že govori MCP namesto prevajanja REST. ``upstream_path`` imena, da gorvodno, kjer živi na lastno vhost aplikacijo, tako da lahko posrednik skriti: doseči ga neposredno hodi mimo seznam dopusta adapter obstaja za uveljavljanje. Ponudnik, ki je v zgornjem toku ločena prikolica ``upstream_network`` namesto tega in nima ničesar za skrivati."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``aliases``: list of DNS aliases. Default: ``[entity_name]`` for shared_net, ``[]`` for default_net"
msgstr "``aliases``: seznam imen DNS. Privzeto: ``[entity_name]`` besedilo shared_net, ``[]`` besedilo default_net"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``allowed`` (default ``True``): the file (or dotted-path entry) MAY be present for a role of this type. Set ``allowed: False`` to forbid the file/entry on roles of this type so the lint layer can surface the offence with a precise reason."
msgstr "``allowed`` (privzeto ``True``): datoteka (ali vnos pikčaste poti) MORDA je prisoten pri vlogi te vrste. Nastavi ``allowed: False`` prepoved dostopa do dokumentacije/vstopa v zvezi z vlogami te vrste, tako da lahko plast line prekrška odkrije z natančnim razlogom."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible_facts`` only carries ``docker0`` once the daemon has run, and the daemon config is written before that on a fresh node - facts are gathered at play start, and nothing re-gathers them after the install. Reading the fact alone therefore yields nothing on the very run that has to emit the address, which leaves the inner containers pointed at the clearnet resolver and the DinD DNS check failing on a domain only the node dnsmasq knows."
msgstr "``ansible_facts`` samo za prevoz ``docker0`` ko demon teče, in demon konfig je napisan pred tem na sveže vozlišče - dejstva so zbrani na začetku igre, in nič jih ponovno zbira po namestitvi. Že samo branje dejstva torej ne daje ničesar na samem zagonu, ki mora oddajati naslov, kar prepušča notranje posode, ki so kazale na razreševalnik bistrega omrežja in DIND DNS preverjanje ne uspe na domeni samo vozlišče dnsmasq ve."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default)"
msgstr "``ansible`` (privzeto)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default) wraps `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD). MDAD runs ~70 upstream sub-roles to deliver Synapse, Element, every supported bridge, Element Call, and Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus pins MDAD by commit, renders an MDAD inventory from ``services.matrix.*`` knobs, and disables MDAD’s bundled Traefik / Postgres / Redis so the central Infinito services back the stack."
msgstr "``ansible`` (privzeto) ovoji `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD). MDAD teče ~70 Povodnjaki za dostavo Synapse, Element, vsak podprt most, Element Call in Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus zatiči MDAD z zavezo, naredi popis MDAD iz ``services.matrix.*`` gumbi, in onemogoči MDAD je paket Traefik / Postgres / Redis Torej, centralne storitve Infinito nazaj kup."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` is the public S3 endpoint and is reachable without SSO gating."
msgstr "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` javni S3 končna točka in je dosegljiva brez SSO gating."

# translation-refused: libretranslate protected-span lost=[] gained=['"']
# nocheck: url
# translation-rejected: ``application_id`` se bere iz spremenljivk igre, razen
# če je podano kot ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` poimenuj blok namesto
# ``ports``, za Discourse"Zaganjalna datoteka", katere ``expose:`` Seznam je
# tisto, kar postane ``docker run -p`` Tako.
msgid "``application_id`` is read from the play variables unless given as ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` names the block instead of ``ports``, for Discourse's launcher file, whose ``expose:`` list is what becomes ``docker run -p`` there."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` of the client doing the discovery."
msgstr "``application_id`` od stranke, ki je to odkrila."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Domov Pomočnik obsega žeton na račun, ki ga je koval. Ta naloga je za administratorja, zato pride klic kot administrator, ki je vprašal stranko. Izpostavljenost entiteti še vedno omejuje doseg. Priti do strežnika orodja je vstavljeno na vlogi ``mcp`` RBAC skupina."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account’s rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Najpomembneje veže klic z računom pripada žeton. Ta razporeditev kovnice, da osebni dostop žeton za administratorski račun, tako klici pridejo s pravicami tega računa, kdorkoli je vprašal. Doseganje orodnega strežnika je nastavljeno na vlogi ``mcp`` RBAC skupina."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the API token is issued against the administrator account, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: API Žeton se izda proti administratorskemu računu, zato ima vsak klic pravice tega računa ne glede na to, kdo je vprašal stranko. Doseganje orodnega strežnika je nastavljeno na vlogi ``mcp`` Skupina RBAC, ki je ločena subvencija od upravljanja Jenkins."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the personal access token is minted against the ``root`` account and stored under the ``administrator`` key, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: osebni dostop žeton je skovan proti ``root`` račun in shranjen pod ``administrator`` ključ, tako da vsak klic nosi pravice tega računa ne glede na to, kdo je vprašal stranko. Doseganje orodnega strežnika je nastavljeno na vlogi ``mcp`` Skupina RBAC, ki je ločena subvencija od upravljanja GitLab."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account’s rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: se spletni servisni žeton izda zoper administratorski račun, tako da ima klic pravice tega računa ne glede na to, kdo je vprašal stranko. Priložene funkcije so samo branje, ki omejuje, kaj lahko te pravice tukaj storijo. Doseganje orodnega strežnika je nastavljeno na vlogi ``mcp`` RBAC skupina."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter’s allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``. Klic prispe na Baserow kot lastnik končne točke ne glede na to, kdo je vprašal stranko, in doseže samo en delovni prostor, ki je lastnik računa. To je druga vez pod adapterjevim seznamom, ne nadomestek zanj."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` Skupina RBAC, ki je ločena od holdinga Nextcloud račun."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject``:    identity MCP calls execute as. ``user`` and ``oidc`` additionally require a ``delegation`` block, because a rendered deployment bearer is a service account no matter what the metadata claims."
msgstr "``auth_subject``: identiteta MCP klice izvršiti kot. ``user`` ter ``oidc`` dodatno zahteva ``delegation`` blok, ker je točen nosilec uporabe račun storitev, ne glede na to, kaj metapodatki trdijo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_type: bearer`` with the token from the discovery data"
msgstr "``auth_type: bearer`` z žetonom iz podatkov o odkritju"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth``:            authentication scheme guarding the endpoint."
msgstr "``auth``: overovitvena shema, ki varuje končno točko."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auto`` is advisory and never fails the unit — every refusal is logged to the journal as ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, so check there if a host you expect to snapshot does not. A stated ``btrfs``/``zfs`` fails the unit instead, which is the point of stating it. Before every snapshot the launcher also removes the ``.baudolo-*`` leftovers a killed run leaves inside the data root."
msgstr "``auto`` je svetovalna in nikoli ne uspe enoti – vsaka zavrnitev se zabeleži v dnevnik kot ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, tako da preverite tam, če gostitelj pričakujete, da posnetek ne. A navedeno ``btrfs``/``zfs`` ne uspe enoti, kar je bistvo navedbe. Pred vsakim posnetek lanser odstrani tudi ``.baudolo-*`` Ostane v korenini podatkov."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``backend``: ``cloud`` or ``chezmoi``"
msgstr "``backend``: ``cloud`` ali ``chezmoi``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``base_dir`` (string): base directory for CA files"
msgstr "``base_dir`` (niz): osnovni imenik za datoteke CA"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``baudolo-restore --empty`` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays the dump in the next, so a consumer that boots in between recreates the schema and the replay dies on its own ``CREATE TABLE``. Hence the refusal while a consumer is up."
msgstr "``baudolo-restore --empty`` pred-čisti shemo v eni seji psql in ponovno predvaja smetišče v naslednji, tako da potrošnik, ki škorenj med poustvarja shema in replay umre sam ``CREATE TABLE``. Zato zavrnitev, medtem ko je potrošnik buden."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``bench new-site`` uses the central MariaDB’s ``root`` to create the per-site DB on first deploy."
msgstr "``bench new-site`` uporablja osrednjo MariaDB’ ``root`` ustvariti DB na kraju samem ob prvi uporabi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``biber`` only ever exists inside EspoCRM through OIDC auto-provisioning (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run in every variant."
msgstr "``biber`` Samo v sebi obstaja. EspoCRM preko samodejnega zagotavljanja OIDC (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` osebe, ki delujejo v vsaki varianti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``bond`` states how tightly a role couples to the service it declares: ``>= 1`` keeps the partner on the same host, ``< 1`` lets it live on its own. The value sits on the consumer's side of the relation, so the pair is directed and the two directions of one pair need not agree."
msgstr "``bond`` navaja, kako tesno vlogo pari za storitev, ki jo razglaša: ``>= 1`` ohranja partnerja na istem gostitelju, ``< 1`` Naj živi sam. Vrednost je na strani potrošnika v razmerju, zato je par usmerjen in dvema smerema enega para ni potrebno soglasje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **parent** ``wiki.example.com`` (plus ``example.com`` apex)"
msgstr "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **matična** ``wiki.example.com`` (plus ``example.com`` apex)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ca_cert_host`` is where sys-ca-selfsigned provisions the root CA on the host. The container-side bind-mount targets live in the ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / ``inject_wrapper_container``) and reach the standalone runtime scripts as env vars and CLI arguments."
msgstr "``ca_cert_host`` kjer je sys-ca-selfsigned določa koren CA za gostitelja. Meje, ki se vežejo na posodo, živijo v ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / ``inject_wrapper_container``) in doseči samostojne scenarije časa delovanja kot env vars in CLI argumenti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``canonical_domain`` is the host of ``canonical_url``, not the configured domain, so both follow the onion substitution a Tor deployment applies. A consumer that compares it against what a page actually renders would otherwise never match on an onion host."
msgstr "``canonical_domain`` je gostitelj ``canonical_url``, ni konfigurirana domena, tako da oba sledita zamenjavi čebule uporaba Tor. Potrošnik, ki jo primerja s tistim, kar stran dejansko naredi, se sicer ne bi nikoli ujemala z gostiteljem čebule."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``central_mariadb_root_password``: The root password for the MariaDB server."
msgstr "``central_mariadb_root_password``: Root geslo za MariaDB strežnik."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``cert_host`` (string): host path to Root CA certificate"
msgstr "``cert_host`` (niz): pot gostitelja do potrdila Root CA"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``classification``:  what this role is in the MCP audit. Required."
msgstr "``classification``: kakšna je ta vloga pri reviziji MCP. Zahtevano."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``comments`` is the parsed per-key comment map from default.env (see :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Dynamic keys carry their comments via each handler's ``COMMENT`` constant. ``custom.env`` overrides run last (see :func:`apply_custom_env`)."
msgstr "``comments`` je razčlenjena na ključ zemljevid komentarja iz default.env (glej :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Dinamični ključi nosijo svoje komentarje preko vsakega obdelovalca ``COMMENT`` Nenehno. ``custom.env`` Povozi zadnji zagon (glej :func:`apply_custom_env`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose build`` re-bakes the static output whenever the cloned content changes, so deploys are content-driven without any runtime build step."
msgstr "``compose build`` ponovno zavre statični izhod vsakič, ko se klonirana vsebina spremeni, zato se razporedi na vsebino, ne da bi prišlo do graditve časa delovanja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose.cache-consumer.yml.j2``, ``apt.list.j2``, ``npmrc.j2`` and ``pip.conf.j2`` under ``templates/``, and the shell scripts under ``files/``, belong to the development compose stack, which drives them through `render.py <../../utils/cache/render.py>`__ and `compose.py <../../cli/administration/deploy/development/compose.py>`__. The Ansible deployment reads none of them."
msgstr "``compose.cache-consumer.yml.j2``, ``apt.list.j2``, ``npmrc.j2`` ter ``pip.conf.j2`` pod ``templates/``, in lupinske skripte pod ``files/``, pripadajo razvoj sklada, ki jih poganja skozi `render.py <../../utils/cache/render.py>`__ ter `compose.py <../../cli/administration/deploy/development/compose.py>`__. Nevidna razporeditev ne bere nobene od njih."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` (deprecated)"
msgstr "``compose`` (amortizirani)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` is the in-repo Docker Compose stack. It remains installable but receives no new features."
msgstr "``compose`` in- repo Docker Compose kup. To ostaja instalable, vendar ne prejema novih funkcij."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` or ``swarm`` to pin every image to that track, ``rotate`` to split the images across both."
msgstr "``compose`` ali ``swarm`` Prilepiti vsako sliko na to skladbo, ``rotate`` Razdeliti slike na oba."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``composer install`` failed."
msgstr "``composer install`` Spodletelo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``config.access_grants: []``, administrator-only rather than public"
msgstr "``config.access_grants: []``, samo administrator in ne javni"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``consumer_not_allowed`` is a decision and simply narrows the result. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` and ``tools_unenforceable`` mean the provider did authorize this consumer and the connection still cannot be rendered, so they abort the run instead of disappearing quietly: a client that silently ends up with fewer tools than the deployment declared is indistinguishable from one that works."
msgstr "``consumer_not_allowed`` je odločitev in preprosto zmanjšuje rezultat. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` ter ``tools_unenforceable`` pomeni, da je ponudnik odobril tega potrošnika in povezave še vedno ni mogoče izvesti, zato prekinejo vožnjo, namesto da bi tiho izginili: stranka, ki molče konča z manj orodji, kot je prijavljena uvedba, se ne razlikuje od tiste, ki deluje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``consumer``: optional override"
msgstr "``consumer``: neobvezna razveljavitev"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``container system prune -a -f`` to remove unused Docker resources."
msgstr "``container system prune -a -f`` odstraniti neporabljene vire zdravila Docker."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``core`` for every language but the source language, ``docs`` for the languages LibreTranslate supports."
msgstr "``core`` za vsak jezik razen izvirnega, ``docs`` za jezike LibreTranslate podporo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credential_missing`` is the one authorized rejection that does not abort, because a provider deploying later in the same play has not written its secret yet. That exemption ends at the reconciliation stage, which runs once every provider has: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` treats it as fatal there."
msgstr "``credential_missing`` je tista odobrena zavrnitev, ki ne prekine, ker ponudnik, ki se razporedi kasneje v isti igri, še ni napisal svoje skrivnosti. Ta izjema se konča v fazi usklajevanja, ki poteka, ko vsak ponudnik: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` Tam je usodno."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credential``:      which principal the provider authenticates as, and where its secret is read from. Replaces the administrator token path."
msgstr "``credential``: kateri glavni ponudnik potrjuje kot in od kod se bere njegova skrivnost. Zamenja administratorjevo pot."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credentials.mcp_bearer``, sent as ``Authorization: Bearer <bearer>``"
msgstr "``credentials.mcp_bearer``, poslano kot ``Authorization: Bearer <bearer>``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``custom.env`` is the operator's untracked override file; its values win over static defaults AND handler-computed values."
msgstr "``custom.env`` je upravljalčeva nesledna datoteka za upravljanje; njene vrednosti zmagajo nad statičnimi privzetimi vrednostmi IN vrednostmi, izračunanimi z upravljalnikom."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_name``: The name of the initial database to create."
msgstr "``database_name``: Ime začetne baze podatkov za ustvarjanje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_password``: The password for the database user."
msgstr "``database_password``: Geslo za uporabnika zbirke podatkov."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_username``: The username for the database user."
msgstr "``database_username``: Uporabniško ime za uporabnika zbirke podatkov."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``days`` (int): certificate validity"
msgstr "``days`` (int): veljavnost potrdila"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``default-address-pools`` is where docker takes that address from, so the declaration answers before the daemon exists and answers identically afterwards. That also keeps daemon.json byte-identical across passes, which the fact-derived value could not: it appeared only from the second run on and restarted the container runtime under a live stack."
msgstr "``default-address-pools`` je, od kod docker vzame ta naslov, zato deklaracija odgovori, preden demon obstaja, in nato odgovarja enako. To tudi drži. daemon.json Byte-identična čez prehode, ki jih vrednost fact-pridobljena ni mogla: prikazala se je samo od drugega teče naprej in ponovno pognala čas teče posode pod živo kup."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``delegation``:      recorded proof, at one exact upstream version, that per-user token acquisition, refresh, audience binding and revocation exist."
msgstr "``delegation``: zabeležen dokaz, na eni točni zgornji različici, da na uporabnika žeton pridobivanje, osvežitev, občinstvo zavezujoče in preklic obstaja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``deployment`` restricts to roles present anywhere in ``groups``, which is what a container-network consumer can actually reach; ``all`` returns every declaring role, deployed or not."
msgstr "``deployment`` omejuje na vloge, prisotne kjer koli v ``groups``, kar je tisto, kar lahko potrošnik omrežja zabojnikov dejansko doseže; ``all`` vrne vsako prijavljeno vlogo, uporabljeno ali ne."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dest``: destination path (required for ``cloud``)"
msgstr "``dest``: ciljna pot (se zahteva za ``cloud``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``direction``:       whether the role exposes MCP, consumes it, or both."
msgstr "``direction``: ali vloga izpostavlja MCP, ga porabi, ali oboje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``discourse``: the WP->Discourse post round-trip scenario. Disabling Discourse skips it; front-page reachability and CSP baselines stay active."
msgstr "``discourse``: WP->Discourse scenarij za povratno vožnjo. Onemogočanje Discourse preskoči; dosegljivost na prvi strani in izhodiščne vrednosti CSP ostanejo aktivne."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``docker_name``    the explicit ``name:`` field (alias for ``name``"
msgstr "``docker_name`` Izrecno ``name:`` polje (druga imena za ``name``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``domains``: canonical and alias domains"
msgstr "``domains``: domene kanonike in vzdevkov"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_apply`` (default: ``true``): run ``doli pull`` after adding mappings"
msgstr "``dotlinker_apply`` (privzeto: ``true``): tek ``doli pull`` po dodajanju kartografij"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_cli_name`` (default: ``doli``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_cli_name`` (privzeto: ``doli``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_config_path`` (default: ``~/.config/dotlinker/config.yaml``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_config_path`` (privzeto: ``~/.config/dotlinker/config.yaml``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_package_name`` (default: ``doli``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_package_name`` (privzeto: ``doli``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_replace`` (default: ``true``): pass ``--replace`` to ``doli add``"
msgstr "``dotlinker_replace`` (privzeto: ``true``): mimo ``--replace`` do ``doli add``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_user`` (required): user to run ``doli`` as"
msgstr "``dotlinker_user`` (zahtevano): uporabnik za zagon ``doli`` kot"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dsk-gnt-cursor`` and ``dsk-gnt-pi`` carry no entry in that map. Cursor is a full editor rather than an extension, and neither vendor publishes an extension on Open VSX, so there is nothing to install into Code for them. Both agents are used from their own binary."
msgstr "``dsk-gnt-cursor`` ter ``dsk-gnt-pi`` Na zemljevidu ni vstopa. Cursor je popoln urednik namesto razširitve, in noben prodajalec ne objavi razširitev na Open VSX, tako da ni ničesar za namestitev v Code Za njih. Oba agenta se uporabljata iz lastne binarne."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``enabled`` (bool)"
msgstr "``enabled`` (bool)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``endpoint``:        connection metadata for clients (server roles only)."
msgstr "``endpoint``: metapodatki o povezavi za stranke (samo vloge strežnikov)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``enforced`` onions every capable row, ``disabled`` none, ``exclusive`` drops the rows that cannot take one, ``auto`` rotates."
msgstr "``enforced`` čebulo vseh sposobnih vrst, ``disabled`` brez, ``exclusive`` spusti vrste, ki ne morejo vzeti ene, ``auto`` Vrti se."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entries_only=true`` returns those strings as a list instead of the rendered block, for a container that is not described by a compose file at all: ``web-app-discourse`` is built by discourse_docker's ``launcher``, whose only argument surface is ``docker_args:`` in its ``app.yml``, so it needs ``--add-host=<entry>`` lines."
msgstr "``entries_only=true`` vrne te nize kot seznam namesto prevedenega bloka, za posodo, ki ni opisana s komponirano datoteko sploh: ``web-app-discourse`` ga gradi discourse_docker's ``launcher``, katerih edina površina argumenta je ``docker_args:`` v svojem ``app.yml``, tako da potrebuje ``--add-host=<entry>`` linije."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entries`` is a list of dotted-path facts about the file's content. Each entry carries the same ``mandatory`` and ``allowed`` semantics described above and adds a ``marker`` flag (default ``False``): ``marker: True`` declares the path as the type marker for the surrounding type entry. :func:`utils.roles.type.get_role_types` walks every ``marker: True`` entry; each marker that resolves to a non-empty value in the role's file adds the surrounding type to the role's type set. ``application_id`` for ``application`` and ``system_service_id`` for ``system-service`` are the canonical markers."
msgstr "``entries`` je seznam pikčastih dejstev o vsebini datoteke. Vsak vnos ima enako. ``mandatory`` ter ``allowed`` semantika opisana zgoraj in dodaja ``marker`` zastava (privzeto ``False``): ``marker: True`` razglasi pot za označevalca tipa za okoliški vnos tipa. :func:`utils.roles.type.get_role_types` hodi vsak ``marker: True`` vnos; vsak označevalec, ki se odloči za neprazno vrednost v datoteki vloge, doda okoliško vrsto na vrsto vloge. ``application_id`` besedilo ``application`` ter ``system_service_id`` besedilo ``system-service`` so kanonični označevalci."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` declares a ``run-name:`` that interpolates the dispatch inputs. Once a run has started, that title is the only record of them: the REST API answers ``inputs: null`` for a workflow_dispatch run. Anything that wants to know what a run was dispatched with therefore parses the title — and parsing it against a hand-copied format would drift the moment the workflow changes, silently and without a failing test."
msgstr "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` razglasi a ``run-name:`` ki interpolira vhode v odpošiljanje. Ko se začne tek, je ta naslov edini rekord: REST API Odgovori ``inputs: null`` za a workflow_dispatch Teci. Vse, kar želi vedeti, kaj je bilo odposlano z zato razčlenjuje naslov – in ga razčleni na ročno kopirani format bi zdrsnil v trenutku, ko se delovni tok spremeni, tiho in brez neuspešnega testa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ephemeral`` publishes the container port on a host port docker picks, for a service addressed only through the compose network."
msgstr "``ephemeral`` objavi kontejnerska vrata na nabiralniku gostiteljskih vrat, za storitev, ki se obravnava samo prek omrežja sestavljanja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``exposed`` is an explicit per-service opt-in (default false) that makes the service reachable over the node onion: its port gets a dedicated ``HiddenServicePort``. Because ``applications`` is the variant-merged config (base ``meta/services.yml`` deep-merged with the round's ``meta/variants.yml`` override), a service is forwarded only in the variant/config where it sets ``exposed: true`` — which is exactly what lets the two DB variants be tested over Tor (v0 exposed -> reachable, v1 not -> refused)."
msgstr "``exposed`` je izrecna možnost za posamezno storitev (privzeto napačno) zaradi česar je storitev dosegljiva preko čebule: njeno pristanišče dobi posvečeno ``HiddenServicePort``. Ker... ``applications`` je config, sestavljen iz variante (osnova ``meta/services.yml`` Globoko zmečkana z rundo. ``meta/variants.yml`` razveljavi), se storitev posreduje samo v varianti/zaupnici, kjer določa ``exposed: true`` – kar je točno to, kar omogoča testiranje obeh variant DB nad Tor (v0 izpostavljeni -> dosegljivi, v1 ne -> zavrnjen)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``exposure``:        who may reach the endpoint."
msgstr "``exposure``: ki lahko dosežejo končni cilj."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``extra_hosts=``, whatever the call site needs on top: a peer's overlay VIP, or a partner service reachable only on the host."
msgstr "``extra_hosts=``, ne glede na to, kaj klicna stran potrebuje na vrhu: Prekrivni VIP vrstnikov, ali partner storitev dosegljiv samo na gostitelju."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``false`` while MCP servers are discovered"
msgstr "``false`` medtem ko so odkrite strežniki MCP"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``family`` is the ``os_family`` ansible reports for the host. Callers that have facts (the action plugin) pass it, so distributions outside the CI matrix - Manjaro, Mint, Rocky - still resolve through their family. Callers without facts (lints, the availability test) omit it and the family is derived from :data:`DISTRO_FAMILY`, which only covers the default matrix."
msgstr "``family`` je ``os_family`` poročila za gostitelja. Klicatelji z dejstvi (vstavek za dejanjeName) Mimo nje, tako da porazdelitev zunaj CI matrice - Manjaro, Mint, Rocky - še vedno rešuje skozi svojo družino. Klicatelji brez dejstev (linte, test razpoložljivosti) izpustite ga in družina izvira iz :data:`DISTRO_FAMILY`, ki zajema samo privzeto matrico."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``filer.seaweedfs.s3.*`` serves the filer web UI behind an admin-only oauth2-proxy."
msgstr "``filer.seaweedfs.s3.*`` služi datotečni spletni uporabniški vmesnik za admin-le oauth2- Proxy."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/configure-auth.sh`` (run on the deploy host) completes the first-run wizard (seeds the break-glass admin), installs both plugins via Jellyfin’s own ``/Packages`` installer, writes the plugin configs, and restarts."
msgstr "``files/configure-auth.sh`` (zažene gostitelja razporeditve) konča čarovnika prvega teka (seme break-glass admin), namesti oba vstavka preko Jellyfinlastne ``/Packages`` monter, piše plugin configs, in ponovno zažene."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/playwright.config.js``: shared Playwright configuration"
msgstr "``files/playwright.config.js``: skupna nastavitev Playwright"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/python/policy.py`` validates it at startup. A contract missing a limit, carrying an empty allowlist, naming a wildcard path or lacking a pinned schema hash is refused before the process serves anything."
msgstr "``files/python/policy.py`` Potrdi ga ob zagonu. Pogodba, ki manjka omejitev, nosi prazen seznam dovoljenj, imenuje pot divje karte ali manjka vezanega hašiša sheme, se zavrne, preden postopek služi karkoli."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``flags``: list of flags to AND. Default: ``[enabled, shared]``"
msgstr "``flags``: seznam zastav za IN. Privzeto: ``[enabled, shared]``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``flavor`` picks the probe shape (see utils/docker/healthcheck/); each flavor brings its own interval, timeout, retries and start_period, and any of those may be overridden next to it. Without a ``flavor`` the entry must carry an explicit ``test`` argv. ``port_key`` selects another entry below ``ports.internal`` for services that expose their probe on a second port."
msgstr "``flavor`` izbere obliko sonde (glej utils/docker/healthcheck/); vsak okus prinaša svoj interval, odmor, retries in start_period, in kateri koli od teh se lahko preglasijo poleg njega. Brez ``flavor`` Vnos mora biti izrecen ``test`` Argv. ``port_key`` Spodaj izbere drug vnos ``ports.internal`` za storitve, ki izpostavljajo sondo v drugem pristanišču."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``force_regen`` (bool): if true, remove and regenerate key/cert"
msgstr "``force_regen`` (bool): če drži, odstranite in regenerirajte ključ/cert"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``forward[A]`` is the list of provider roles that ``A`` directly depends on (services it embeds). ``reverse[B]`` is the list of roles that directly depend on ``B`` (consumers that embed ``B``)."
msgstr "``forward[A]`` seznam vlog ponudnikov, ki ``A`` neposredno odvisno od (storitve, ki jih vgradi). ``reverse[B]`` seznam vlog, ki so neposredno odvisne od ``B`` (potrošniki, ki so vgradili ``B``)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``galaxy_info.author`` is where a role records who implemented it, so that is where the names are read. A role may credit more than one person, comma separated."
msgstr "``galaxy_info.author`` je, kjer so zapisi o vlogah, ki so ga izvedli, tako da se tam berejo imena. Vloga lahko pripada več kot eni osebi, vejica ločena."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``getent`` honours nsswitch and cannot address a server, so on its own it cannot say which of the resolvers in resolv.conf refused. Where the distro ships a query tool, ask every nameserver directly; where it does not, the per-name verdicts still stand on their own."
msgstr "``getent`` počasti nsswitch in ne more naslov strežnika, zato sam ne more povedati, kateri od reševalcev v resolv.conf odklonil. Kjer distro brodi povpraševalno orodje, vprašajte vsakega imenarja naravnost; kjer ga ne, razsodbe po imenu še stoje same od sebe."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` is the single source of truth for host paths. The env layer (utils/env/handlers, exported by scripts/meta/env/load.sh) derives the ``INFINITO_*`` env keys from it; a set env wins so callers can override. When a tool runs outside that layer, e.g. a bare ``subprocess`` that does not inherit the env build, the value is read straight from the group_vars SPOT, so there is still no hardcoded literal default."
msgstr "``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` je edini vir resnice za gostiteljske poti. Env plast (utils/env/handlers, ki jo izvaža scripts/meta/env/load.sh) izpelje ``INFINITO_*`` Env tipke iz njega; set env zmaga, tako da lahko klicatelji razveljavi. Kadar orodje teče zunaj te plasti, npr. golo ``subprocess`` ki ne podeduje env graditi, vrednost se bere naravnost iz group_vars SPOT, tako da še vedno ni zakodirano dobesedno privzeto."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``host_alias=true``, which pins ``host.docker.internal`` at whatever reaches the host in the effective mode. A container that must talk to a service the host publishes -- msmtp relaying through the swarm ingress on :587, for instance -- needs the alias, and it must not hardcode ``host-gateway`` because that breaks under swarm for the reason below."
msgstr "``host_alias=true``, ki zatiči ``host.docker.internal`` pri čemer koli doseže gostitelja v učinkovitem načinu. Vsebnik, ki mora govoriti s storitvijo, ki jo gostitelj objavi -- msmtp releating skozi roj ingres na:587, na primer -- potrebuje psevdonim in ne sme imeti trde kode ``host-gateway`` Ker se to podre pod rojom iz spodaj navedenega razloga."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``http://giteamcpupstream:8080/mcp``, own network only"
msgstr "``http://giteamcpupstream:8080/mcp``, samo lastno omrežje"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``http://nginx:80/webservice/mcp/server.php`` on the shared MCP overlay"
msgstr "``http://nginx:80/webservice/mcp/server.php`` o skupnem prekrivanju MCP"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``implementation``:  how the surface is provided, ordered by precedence."
msgstr "``implementation``: kako je površina zagotovljena, naročena po prednosti."

# translation-refused: libretranslate protected-span lost=[]
# gained=['root/.msmtprc']
# nocheck: url
# translation-rejected: ``in_container`` obstaja, ker ena predloga služi dvema
# potrošnikoma. Gostitelja / root/.msmtprc prebere gostitelj in zanka nazaj je
# prava zanj; kopija, pritrjena na /etc/msmtprc, se bere znotraj posode, kjer
# 127.0.0.1 Ta zabojnik je povratek in nič ga ne posluša. Taka storitev mora
# oddajati tudi ``lookup('container_extra_hosts')`` Tako se reši psevdonim.
msgid "``in_container`` exists because one template serves two consumers. The host's /root/.msmtprc is read by the host and loopback is right for it; the copy mounted at /etc/msmtprc is read inside a container, where 127.0.0.1 is that container's own loopback and nothing listens on it. Such a service must also emit ``lookup('container_extra_hosts')`` so the alias resolves."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``indent=0`` collapses everything to the left edge - useful when the lookup is rendered into top-level YAML (no service wrapper)."
msgstr "``indent=0`` se zruši vse na levi rob - uporabno, ko je vpogled preveden v zgornji nivo YAML (brez servisnega ovoja)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ingress`` (default) emits the short ``\"host:published:container\"`` string; ``host`` emits the long block with ``mode: host``, which is what an edge role needs in swarm so the client address survives the hop."
msgstr "``ingress`` (privzeto) oddaja kratek ``\"host:published:container\"`` niz; ``host`` oddaja dolg blok z ``mode: host``, ki je tisto, kar rob vlogo potrebuje v roju tako klient naslov preživi hmelj."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``internal`` (default) reads ``ports.internal.<proto>``; ``same`` reuses the published port, for services that cannot remap (STUN/TURN, media relays)."
msgstr "``internal`` (privzeto) bere ``ports.internal.<proto>``; ``same`` ponovno uporabi objavljena vrata za storitve, ki jih ni mogoče ponovno načrtovati (STUN/TURN, medijski releji)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``internal``, container network only"
msgstr "``internal``, samo kontejnersko omrežje"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``kas`` (Kubernetes agent server, workspaces), ``pages``, ``registry`` and ``mailroom`` are not deployed; ``gitlab.yml`` disables them."
msgstr "``kas`` (Strežnik agentov Kubernetes, delovni prostori), ``pages``, ``registry`` ter ``mailroom`` se ne uporabljajo; ``gitlab.yml`` jih onesposobi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key_bits`` (int): RSA key size"
msgstr "``key_bits`` (int): velikost ključa RSA"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key_host`` (string): host path to Root CA private key"
msgstr "``key_host`` (niz): gostiteljska pot do privatnega ključa Root CA"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key`` names the pinned key and defaults to ``version``; an entity with several pins declares a list of such blocks. The types are ``git_tags`` (repository), ``registry_tags`` (image), ``npm`` (package), ``http_regex`` (url, pattern) and ``script`` (path, run with the current version and printing the latest one)."
msgstr "``key`` poimenuje pripeto tipko in privzeto ``version``; subjekt z več zatiči razglasi seznam takšnih blokov. Tipi so ``git_tags`` (Skladišče), ``registry_tags`` (slika), ``npm`` (paket), ``http_regex`` (url, vzorec) ter ``script`` (pot, tek s trenutno različico in tiskanje najnovejše)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key``: services.<key>.* lookup base. Default: provides or entity_name"
msgstr "``key``: storitve.<key>.* V bazi za iskanje. Privzeto: poda ali entity_name"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``kind``: ``services_flags`` (default) | ``database`` | ``mcp_client`` | ``web_facing`` | ``onion_sso``. ``mcp_client`` admits a role only when its ``mcp.direction`` is ``client`` or ``both`` AND it declares ``services.<own-entity>.mcp_consumer: true`` without the provider refusing it through ``mcp_consumer: false`` on that same entry, so a provider's network carries the clients it admitted rather than every client in the deployment. Being a client is not an admission: without the second condition one admission anywhere reaches every provider that opens its overlay."
msgstr "``kind``: ``services_flags`` (privzeto) ``database`` ``mcp_client`` ``web_facing`` ``onion_sso``. ``mcp_client`` priznava vlogo samo, če ``mcp.direction`` m ``client`` ali ``both`` IZJAVA ``services.<own-entity>.mcp_consumer: true`` brez ponudnika, ki ga zavrne ``mcp_consumer: false`` pri istem vnosu, tako da mreža ponudnika nosi stranke, ki jih je sprejel, in ne vse stranke v uvajanju. Biti stranka ni priznanje: brez drugega pogoja en sprejem kjerkoli doseže vsak ponudnik, ki odpre svoj pokrov."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``last`` seeds the OCI pagination cursor: only tags sorting lexically after it are returned. Repos like GitLab CNG carry tens of thousands of commit-sha tags before the ``v*`` release tags, so an unseeded scan exhausts ``max_pages`` without ever reaching them."
msgstr "``last`` Seme OCI pagination kazalec: samo oznake razvrščanje leksikalno, ko se vrne. Repo kot GitLab CNG nosi več deset tisoč tags-sha pred ``v*`` sprostite oznake, tako da nesemenjeni skeniranje izpušnih plinov ``max_pages`` Ne da bi jih dosegel."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``latest`` is the last commit of the default branch. It is built at start and rebuilt whenever a fetch finds a new commit; the previous build stays online until the new one replaces it."
msgstr "``latest`` je zadnja obveznost privzete veje. Zgrajena je na začetku in obnovljena vsakič, ko pridelek najde novo zavezo; prejšnja zgradba ostane na spletu, dokler je nova ne nadomesti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``laya``, ``torch`` or ``onnx``; the role refuses anything else"
msgstr "``laya``, ``torch`` ali ``onnx``; vloga zavrača vse drugo"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ldap``: the three RBAC scenarios additionally depend on LDAP group sync; disabling LDAP skips them alongside OIDC."
msgstr "``ldap``: trije scenariji RBAC so dodatno odvisni od sinhronizacije skupine LDAP; onesposobitev LDAP jih preskoči ob OIDC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ldapauth`` is the only path that materialises a ``friendica.user`` row, so its enablement derives directly from the ``ldap`` service flag. The oauth2-proxy ``sso`` gate in front of the vhost is a front-door auth gate, not an addon bridge, and stays in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. The LDAP login path is covered by the existing LDAP Playwright spec (requirement 018), so no addon-specific spec is added."
msgstr "``ldapauth`` je edina pot, ki se uresniči ``friendica.user`` vrstica, tako da njegova možnost izhaja neposredno iz ``ldap`` Zastava za storitve. Oauth2-proksi ``sso`` Vrata pred vhostom so vhodna vrata, ne addonski most, in ostanejo v ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>` . Prijava LDAP je zajeta z obstoječim LDAP Playwright spec (zahteva 018), tako da ni dodan noben specifičen dodatek."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``libaacs`` (AACS decryption library)"
msgstr "``libaacs`` (Knjižnica za dešifriranje AACS)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``libbluray`` (Blu-ray playback support library)"
msgstr "``libbluray`` (Podporna knjižnica za predvajanje Blu-ray)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lifecycle``  — maturity marker filtered by ``cli meta roles lifecycle``."
msgstr "``lifecycle`` — zapadlost označevalca filtrira z ``cli meta roles lifecycle``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``limits``:          the request, response, timeout, concurrency, pagination and stream ceilings the surface enforces."
msgstr "``limits``: zahteva, odgovor, timeout, soglasje, domišljija in stružni stropi površina uveljavlja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``locale-gen`` only re-runs when the template changes"
msgstr "``locale-gen`` Ponavlja se samo, kadar se spremeni predloga."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``locale.conf``: sets ``LANG`` and ``LANGUAGE`` environment variables"
msgstr "``locale.conf``: setov ``LANG`` ter ``LANGUAGE`` okoljske spremenljivke"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``locale.gen``: uncomment or specify the locales you need"
msgstr "``locale.gen``: uncomment ali navedite krajev, ki jih potrebujete"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``lookup('guide_role', application_id)`` picks the first invokable app the round deployed beside ``application_id``. Invokability comes from :func:`utils.roles.validation.invokable.list_invokable_app_ids`, so no caller re-derives it from role-name prefixes."
msgstr "``lookup('guide_role', application_id)`` izbere prvo invokabilno aplikacijo v krogu poleg ``application_id``. Invokability prihaja iz :func:`utils.roles.validation.invokable.list_invokable_app_ids`, Zato ga noben klicatelj ne prenese iz predpone imen vlog."

