msgstr "``msgctxt`` predpone sporočil, ki jih je treba vključiti, npr. ``role:``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``mutating_proofs``: required once ``tools.mutating_tools_enabled`` is true. Names the artifact proving each of confirmation, authorization, idempotency, audit and reversal for the mutating variant, separately from the read-only one."
msgstr "``mutating_proofs``: se zahteva enkrat ``tools.mutating_tools_enabled`` Res je. Poimenuje artefakt, ki dokazuje vsako potrditev, avtorizacijo, idempotenco, revizijo in obrat za mutirano različico, ločeno od bralne."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``name``           the EFFECTIVE docker volume name"
msgstr "``name`` UČINKOVITO VZORČNO IME"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``name``: unique mapping id"
msgstr "``name``: edinstven identifikator kartiranja"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``networks.internet.dns`` arrives through ``-e @inventories/...`` and is read straight out of ``variables``, which hands back whatever the file contains. While that was a literal address nobody noticed; an expression there reached the daemon as its own source text and docker refused the config with ``ParseAddr(\"{{ ... }}\")``."
msgstr "``networks.internet.dns`` prispe skozi ``-e @inventories/...`` in se bere naravnost iz ``variables``, ki poda nazaj karkoli je v datoteki. Čeprav je bil to dobesedni naslov, ki ga nihče ni opazil; izraz, ki je prišel do demona kot njegovo izvorno besedilo in docker zavrnil konfig z ``ParseAddr(\"{{ ... }}\")``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``new_text_or_None`` is ``None`` when nothing changed."
msgstr "``new_text_or_None`` m ``None`` Ko se ni nič spremenilo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``nfs``            NFS opt-in (bool or dict), ``None`` if absent"
msgstr "``nfs`` Opt-in NFS (bool ali dikt), ``None`` če manjka"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``noqa`` and ``nocheck`` are accepted as synonyms (case-insensitive) by this parser. By repo convention every project rule from ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` MUST use ``nocheck:`` because ``# noqa: <code>`` is also parsed by ruff as a flake8 directive and triggers ``invalid-noqa-code`` warnings on every project-specific rule key. ``noqa:`` is reserved for real flake8 / ruff codes (``E402``, ``F401``, …). The ``direct-yaml`` lint enforces the convention by hard-rejecting the ``noqa:`` form."
msgstr "``noqa`` ter ``nocheck`` sprejeti kot sopomenke (neobčutljiva na velikost črk) Od tega razčlenjevalca. Po repo konvenciji vsak projekt pravilo od ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` MORATE uporabiti ``nocheck:`` ker ``# noqa: <code>`` je tudi razčlenjen z ruff kot kosmiči8 direktiva in sprožilci ``invalid-noqa-code`` opozorila na vsak ključ od pravil za posamezne projekte. ``noqa:`` je rezervirana za prave kosmiče8 / ruff kode (``E402``, ``F401``, ...). O ``direct-yaml`` Lint uveljavlja konvencijo s trdim zavračanjem ``noqa:`` Obrazec."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``offset`` moves that start deliberately: it is how an operator reaches the tail without waiting for anything. It defaults to 0, so every run that does not ask for it deploys the same head and can be compared against the last one. This used to be derived from the sweep number instead, which bought tail coverage at the price of the head -- chunk 0 began wherever the arithmetic pointed, the rows that matter most ran only every few sweeps, and no two runs were comparable."
msgstr "``offset`` poteze, ki se začnejo namerno: je način, kako operater doseže rep, ne da bi čakal na karkoli. Privzeto 0, tako da vsak tek, ki ne prosi za to razporedi isto glavo in se lahko primerja z zadnjim. To je bilo včasih izpeljano iz številke, ki je namesto tega kupila pokritost repa po ceni glave -- delček 0 Začelo se je povsod, kjer je aritmetika kazala, vrste, ki so bile najpomembnejše, so potekale le vsakih nekaj ogledov in nobena dva ni bila primerljiva."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``oidc-authenticator`` and ``ldap-authenticator`` are mutually exclusive auth backends (only one may be enabled; see ```tasks/01_validation.yml`` <./tasks/01_validation.yml>`__), each deriving its enablement from its bridged service flag. The OIDC/LDAP runtime configuration (provider URLs, bind DN, secrets) lives in the XWiki property templates and is read via ``lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')``; the addon ``config:`` carries only the installer coordinate."
msgstr "``oidc-authenticator`` ter ``ldap-authenticator`` so medsebojno izključujoče varnostne hrbtenice (omogočen je lahko samo eden; glej ```tasks/01_validation.yml`` <./tasks/01_validation.yml>`__), each deriving its enablement from its bridged service flag. The OIDC/LDAP runtime configuration (provider URLs, bind DN, secrets) lives in the XWiki property templates and is read via ``lookup('config', application_id, 'secrets.credentials.<name>')``; the addon ``config:`` nosi samo koordinate monterja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``oidc``: baseline admin OIDC round-trip plus the three RBAC scenarios (subscriber/editor/administrator)."
msgstr "``oidc``: izhodiščni administrator OIDC ob koncu in treh scenarijih RBAC (subscriber/editor/administrator)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``openssl_conf_host`` (string): host path for generated openssl.cnf"
msgstr "``openssl_conf_host`` (niz): pot gostitelja za ustvarjeno openssl.cnf"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``out`` itself lives under the dump dir (both derive from INFINITO_RESCUE_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR), so the walk must skip its own output subtree or copytree recurses into the growing destination until ENAMETOOLONG."
msgstr "``out`` sam živi pod smetiščem. (oboje izhaja iz INFINITO_RESCUE_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR), tako hoja mora preskočiti svojo izhodno poddrevo ali copytree se ponavlja v rastočo destinacijo do ENAMETOLONG."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``owner/repo`` the branch lives on."
msgstr "``owner/repo`` Veja živi naprej."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``owner/repo`` the run lives in."
msgstr "``owner/repo`` V teku živi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``package.json`` and ``playwright.config.js`` are provided centrally by this role:"
msgstr "``package.json`` ter ``playwright.config.js`` ki jih centralno zagotavlja ta vloga:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``package_name`` (string) Name of the Python package to install (e.g., ``dockreap``, ``backup-docker-to-local``)."
msgstr "``package_name`` (niz) Ime paketa Python za namestitev (Npr. ``dockreap``, ``backup-docker-to-local``)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``password`` (should come from vault/credentials)"
msgstr "``password`` (prihaja iz trezorja/zaupnice)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``path``           the legacy ``path:`` field, ``''`` if absent"
msgstr "``path`` zapuščina ``path:`` polje, ``''`` če manjka"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``phpunit/phpunit`` declares ``_PHPUNIT_EXTENSIONS`` as platform requirements and Composer refuses to resolve the vendor tree without them, so they are part of the toolchain rather than of the suite consuming it. A distro ships them as packages separate from the interpreter, which is why a present ``php`` binary does not imply they are there."
msgstr "``phpunit/phpunit`` razglasi ``_PHPUNIT_EXTENSIONS`` kot zahteve platforme in Sestavljalec zavrača reševanje prodajnega drevesa brez njih, tako da so del orodne verige, ne pa suite, ki ga porabi. Distro jih pošilja kot pakete, ločene od tolmača, zato je sedanjost ``php`` To ne pomeni, da so tam."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``playwright.spec.js`` — orchestrator: TLS baseline, project creation, image asset upload, and the ``guest``/``biber``/``administrator`` personas. The ``biber`` / ``administrator`` personas are declared blocked via ``PERSONA_*_BLOCKED`` (mirroring ``web-app-taiga``): Penpot’s in-app “OpenID” entry and SPA user-menu logout aren’t driveable by the generic persona helper, so both users’ real auth is exercised by the dedicated login companions above."
msgstr "``playwright.spec.js`` — Orkester: TLS osnova, ustvarjanje projektov, nalaganje slikovnih sredstev in ``guest``/``biber``/``administrator`` Personas. – ``biber`` / ``administrator`` osebe so razglašene za blokirane prek ``PERSONA_*_BLOCKED`` (zrcaljenje ``web-app-taiga``): Penpot je in-app “OpenID” vnos in SPA uporabniško-menu odjava niso gonilna s strani splošnega persona pomočnika, tako da je tako uporabniki’ real auth izvaja namenski prijavni spremljevalci zgoraj."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``playwright.version`` in ``meta/services.yml`` is the single source of truth for the default Playwright version; the central ``templates/package.json.j2`` pins it via the ``image_version`` filter."
msgstr "``playwright.version`` v ``meta/services.yml`` je edini vir resnice za privzeto različico Playwright; ``templates/package.json.j2`` zatiči skozi ``image_version`` filter."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``plg_system_keycloak`` is built imperatively inside the Joomla container and speaks OIDC against Keycloak. Its enablement derives directly from the ``sso`` service flag, and its OIDC runtime contract (issuer, client id/secret, redirect/end-session URLs, fallback toggle, and RBAC group paths) lives under the addon’s ``config:`` block, which ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ renders into the ``JOOMLA_OIDC_*`` plugin environment."
msgstr "``plg_system_keycloak`` je nujno zgrajena znotraj Joomla zabojnik in govori OIDC proti Keycloak. Njegova možnost izhaja neposredno iz ``sso`` zastava storitve in pogodba o delu OIDC (izdajatelj, ID odjemalca/tajni, URL-ji za preusmeritev/končno sejo, rezervni toggle in poti skupine RBAC) živi pod addonom ``config:`` blok, ki ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ renders into the ``JOOMLA_OIDC_*`` okolje vstavkov."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``poll: 0`` makes a task fire and forget, so its own ``changed_when`` and ``failed_when`` never see an outcome. The outcome only exists once the job is collected with ``async_status``, and collecting it is where the verdict has to be made -- for a whole batch at once, so one run reports every broken job rather than the first."
msgstr "``poll: 0`` naredi nalogo ogenj in pozabi, tako da svoje ``changed_when`` ter ``failed_when`` Nikoli ne vidiš izida. Rezultat obstaja šele, ko se delo zbere z ``async_status``, in zbiranje je, kjer je treba razsodbo - za celotno serijo naenkrat, tako en teči poroča vsako zlomljeno delo namesto prvega."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ports.onion`` is a category-keyed map of booleans alongside ``internal`` / ``local`` / ``public``: it names which of a service's already-declared ports should answer on the node onion, and nothing else. The port number comes from ``ports.local`` when that category is declared there and from ``ports.public`` otherwise, which is the precedence ``container_ports`` publishes by, so the forward always targets the port the service is actually reachable on."
msgstr "``ports.onion`` je zemljevid boolejev s tipkami kategorije ``internal`` / ``local`` / ``public``: poimenuje, kateri od storitev je že prijavljena pristanišča naj odgovori na vozlišče čebule, in nič drugega. Številka vrat prihaja iz ``ports.local`` kadar je navedena kategorija navedena tam in od ``ports.public`` drugače, kar je prednost ``container_ports`` objavlja, tako da naprej vedno cilja na pristanišče, na katerem je storitev dejansko dosegljiva."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``priority`` IS the retrigger: it names what failed. ``offset`` is recomputed rather than carried, but from the carried value up: the source run got a stretch behind its own offset green before its budget ran out, so the regular line resumes behind that stretch (:func:`cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.resume_offset`) instead of repeating it, and never falls back behind where that run started. Everything else is carried verbatim, including ``whitelist``, so a retrigger of a scoped run stays inside that scope instead of quietly widening to the whole repository."
msgstr "``priority`` JE retrigger: pove, kaj ni uspelo. ``offset`` je recomputirano namesto preneseno, vendar od prenesene vrednosti navzgor: vir teče dobil odsek za lastno izravnavo zeleno, preden je zmanjkalo proračuna, tako da se redna linija nadaljuje za tem odsekom (:func:`cli.administration.deploy.ci.selections.resume_offset`) namesto da bi to ponovil in nikoli ne zaostajal za tem, kjer se je začel ta tek. Vse drugo se nosi dobesedno, vključno ``whitelist``, tako da ponovno sprožilec obsežno teči ostane znotraj tega obsega namesto tiho širi v celotnem skladišču."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``provider`` / ``provider_key``: for ``onion_sso``, the app whose"
msgstr "``provider`` / ``provider_key``: za ``onion_sso``, aplikacija, katere"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``provides`` matching runs in both directions, so a provider (e.g. openldap ``provides: ldap``) is picked up even when the consuming flag uses a ``groups[...]`` form the ``group_names`` regex cannot read."
msgstr "``provides`` ujemanje poteka v obe smeri, tako da ponudnik (npr. openldap ``provides: ldap``) se pobere tudi, če porabi zastavo uporablja ``groups[...]`` oblikuje ``group_names`` regex ne zna brati."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``proxy_aliases``: aliases the beacon exposes for harvesting; falls back"
msgstr "``proxy_aliases``: alias svetilnik izpostavlja za žetev; pade nazaj"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``proxy_pass`` directive; swarm prepends a ``set`` line (request-time DNS)."
msgstr "``proxy_pass`` Direktiva; roj pripravi a ``set`` vrstica (čas za zahtevo DNS)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``proxy_resolvable``: beacon flag - the harvested aliases get attached to"
msgstr "``proxy_resolvable``: zastavica svetilnika - pridobljeni vzdevki se pritrdijo na"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``quay.io/centos/centos:latest`` becomes ``centos:latest``; a two-segment image such as ``debian:13`` is returned unchanged."
msgstr "``quay.io/centos/centos:latest`` postane ``centos:latest``; dvodelna slika, kot je ``debian:13`` se vrne nespremenjena."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``reason``:          why a non-deployable classification cannot serve."
msgstr "``reason``: zakaj neuresničljiva klasifikacija ne more služiti."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``relay`` and ``media`` are UDP. ``stun_turn`` and its TLS variant do speak TCP, but the allocation they hand out is a UDP relay address the onion client can never receive on, so forwarding the signalling port buys nothing."
msgstr "``relay`` ter ``media`` so UDP. ``stun_turn`` in njegova TLS različica ne govorijo TCP, vendar dodelitev, ki jo delijo je UDP rele naslov čebule odjemalec nikoli ne more dobiti na, tako posredovanje signalizacija vrata kupi nič."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``repo`` carries the repository the names come from, defined inline on the entry that needs it: a full definition (``name``/``description``/ ``baseurl``/``gpgkey``) rendered as a yum repo, ``bootstrap_package`` for a repo shipped as a package such as ``epel-release``, ``enable_existing`` to switch on a repo the distro already ships, ``pacman_section`` to uncomment a section of ``pacman.conf`` such as ``multilib``, ``copr``/``ppa`` for a community repository, or ``managed_externally`` when the role sets it up itself."
msgstr "``repo`` ima skladišče, iz katerega prihajajo imena, opredeljena v vrstici, ki jo potrebuje: popolna opredelitev (``name``/``description``/ ``baseurl``/``gpgkey``) pretvorjeno kot jum repo, ``bootstrap_package`` za repo blago, poslano kot paket, kot je ``epel-release``, ``enable_existing`` vklopiti repo že distro ladje, ``pacman_section`` Odobriti del ``pacman.conf`` kot so ``multilib``, ``copr``/``ppa`` za repozitorij skupnosti ali ``managed_externally`` Ko se vloga sama postavi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``repos`` or ``upstreams``."
msgstr "``repos`` ali ``upstreams``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``required`` (always installed)"
msgstr "``required`` (vedno nameščen)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``required`` (always installed, vendored)"
msgstr "``required`` (vedno nameščen, prodan)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``requirepass`` for the ``default`` (admin) user, sourced from the ``REDIS_PASSWORD`` credential."
msgstr "``requirepass`` za ``default`` (admin) uporabnik, pridobljen iz ``REDIS_PASSWORD`` Zaupnica."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``retries`` counts CONSECUTIVE failures, and a request that leaves the container is load balanced across the service VIP. With N replicas and one of them alive, a round robin never produces more than N-1 failures in a row, so a streak based check is arithmetically blind to losing all but one backend. Chaining ``samples`` requests into a single probe makes one probe cover the whole pool instead."
msgstr "``retries`` Štetje KONSEKUTIVNE napake, in zahteva, da zapusti posodo je obremenitev uravnotežena po storitvi VIP. Z N replikami in eno živo, okrogla taščica nikoli ne proizvede več kot N-1 napake v vrsti, tako da proga temelji preverjanje je aritmetično slepa, da izgubi vse razen ene hrbtenice. Veriženje ``samples`` Ena sonda prekrije ves bazen."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``role`` may be a role name (relative to ``roles/``) or an absolute path to a role directory. Pass ``role_name`` explicitly when ``role`` is an arbitrary path whose basename is not the canonical role name."
msgstr "``role`` je lahko ime vloge (glede na ``roles/``) ali absolutno pot do imenika vlog. Premik ``role_name`` izrecno ``role`` je samovoljna pot, katere osnovno ime ni ime kanonične vloge."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/<app>/meta/server.yml`` declares ``status_codes`` keyed like ``domains.canonical``; it is the single source of truth for every prober."
msgstr "``roles/<app>/meta/server.yml`` razglasi ``status_codes`` kot ``domains.canonical``; To je edini vir resnice za vsakega sonderja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/<application_id>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`` Follow `Contributing ``playwright.env.j2`` <../../docs/agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md>`__ and `Contributing ``playwright.spec.js`` <../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/role/playwright.specs.js.md>`__ while creating them."
msgstr "``roles/<application_id>/files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`` Sledi `Contributing ``playwright.env.j2`` <../../docs/agents/files/role/playwright.env.j2.md>`__ ter `Contributing ``playwright.spec.js`` <../../docs/contributing/artefact/files/role/playwright.specs.js.md>`__ med ustvarjanjem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/sys-lint/meta/services.yml`` is the SPOT for both the repository and the version of every GitHub-release lint tool. Each entry carries the ``repository`` / ``ref`` pair that ``utils.update.repository`` already scans, so the existing ``update-repository-refs`` CI job bumps the pins to the latest semver tag and opens a PR -- the same machinery that keeps ``roles/pkgmgr`` current."
msgstr "``roles/sys-lint/meta/services.yml`` je SPOT tako za skladišče in različico vsakega GitHub-release lint orodje. Vsak vnos ima ``repository`` / ``ref`` par, ki ``utils.update.repository`` Že skenira, tako da obstoječi ``update-repository-refs`` Integrirana delovna mesta se zaletijo v zadnji semver in odprejo PR - isti stroj, ki drži ``roles/pkgmgr`` tok."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/playwright.config.js`` (copied as-is)"
msgstr "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/files/playwright.config.js`` (kopiran kot je)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/templates/package.json.j2`` (rendered per-deploy; pins ``@playwright/test`` from ``meta/services.yml.playwright.version``)"
msgstr "``roles/test-e2e-playwright/templates/package.json.j2`` (izdelani po razgradnji; zatiči ``@playwright/test`` od ``meta/services.yml.playwright.version``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``roles_with_service('mcp', direction='server')`` entries."
msgstr "``roles_with_service('mcp', direction='server')`` vnosi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``run_after``  — project-specific role-load-order list."
msgstr "``run_after`` — seznam nalogov za nalaganje za posamezne projekte."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``run_after`` is deliberately NOT read: it is a deploy-ordering hint, not a runtime dependency. The wider cosmos (federation peers, external bridged networks) cannot be derived from metadata and is left for the author to add."
msgstr "``run_after`` se namerno NE bere: je namig za razporeditev, ne pa odvisnost od časa delovanja. Širši kozmos (vrstniki federacij, zunanja premostitvena omrežja) ni mogoče izpeljati iz metapodatkov in je prepuščen avtorju, da doda."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``scripts/lint/packages.sh`` validates the generated packaging metadata with each ecosystem's native parser. This installer provisions those parsers wherever the platform's package manager can: on Debian (apt) the lint container gets ``dpkg-parsechangelog`` (``dpkg-dev``), ``rpmspec`` (``rpm``) and ``rpmlint``; on Arch (pacman) a dev host gets ``namcap``."
msgstr "``scripts/lint/packages.sh`` potrdi ustvarjene metapodatke o embalaži z domačim razčlenjevalcem vsakega ekosistema. Ta monter zagotavlja, da razčlenjevalniki kjerkoli lahko paket upravitelj platforme: na Debian (apt) Posoda za lino dobi ``dpkg-parsechangelog`` (``dpkg-dev``), ``rpmspec`` (``rpm``) ter ``rpmlint``; na Archu (pacman) Dev gostitelj dobi ``namcap``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``semantic_name``  the YAML key from ``meta/volumes.yml``"
msgstr "``semantic_name`` ključ YAML od ``meta/volumes.yml``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.<provider_key>.enabled`` must also hold. Default provider_key ``tor``"
msgstr "``services.<provider_key>.enabled`` morajo tudi zdržati. Privzeto provider_key ``tor``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.code.flavor`` picks one of ``code-oss``, ``vscodium`` or ``vscode``. The three builds conflict at package level, so the role removes the other two before installing the chosen one."
msgstr "``services.code.flavor`` izbere enega od ``code-oss``, ``vscodium`` ali ``vscode``. Tri gradi konflikt na ravni paketa, tako da vloga odstrani druga dva pred namestitvijo izbranega."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.libretranslate``: image and version"
msgstr "``services.libretranslate``: podoba in različica"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.litellm.remote_models`` already narrowed to the providers this host holds a key for. An entry whose provider is ``mock`` answers from its own ``response`` and calls nothing."
msgstr "``services.litellm.remote_models`` Ta gostitelj že ima ključ za ponudnike. Vnos, katerega ponudnik je ``mock`` odgovori iz lastnih ``response`` in ne kliče ničesar."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.matomo``: enable analytics"
msgstr "``services.matomo``: omogoči analitiko"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.matrix.conferencing.element_call`` and ``services.matrix.conferencing.jitsi`` toggle MDAD’s Element Call / Jitsi stacks (ansible flavor only). Both default to true."
msgstr "``services.matrix.conferencing.element_call`` ter ``services.matrix.conferencing.jitsi`` Preklopi klic elementa MDAD / Jitsi nizov (samo neužiten okus). Oba sta privzeta."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.openwebui.embedding_model``, ``.image_model``, ``.speech_to_text_model`` and ``.text_to_speech_model`` route embeddings, images, speech recognition and speech synthesis through the gateway; an embedding model set here also replaces the sentence-transformer the image otherwise downloads from Hugging Face on first start"
msgstr "``services.openwebui.embedding_model``, ``.image_model``, ``.speech_to_text_model`` ter ``.text_to_speech_model`` traus vgradnje, slike, prepoznavanje govora in sinteza govora skozi prehod; model vgradnje, ki je nastavljen tukaj, nadomešča tudi stavek-prevajalnik sicer prenese iz Hugging Face na prvi začetek"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.redis``: enable Redis backend"
msgstr "``services.redis``: omogoči Redis hrbtenica"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.s1.flavor`` selects which implementation answers that contract. ``laya`` runs `Laya <https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya>`__, the default; ``torch`` and ``onnx`` run `jeff <https://github.com/logan-markewich/jeff>`__ over a GLiFormer encoder, which is what the role carried before. Neither upstream ships a container image, so the role builds one and bakes the checkpoints into it. Baking keeps the deploy free of a download at container start, which is the failure mode a sibling role’s model pull already hit."
msgstr "``services.s1.flavor`` izbere, katera izvedba odgovarja na to pogodbo. ``laya`` teče `Laya <https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya>`__, privzeto; ``torch`` ter ``onnx`` Poženi `jeff <https://github.com/logan-markewich/jeff>`__ preko kodirnika GLiFormer, kar je bila vloga prej. Niti gornje ladje ne slikajo zabojnikov, zato vloga enega naredi in vanj spečeš kontrolne točke. Pečenje ohranja razporeditev brez prenosa ob zagonu zabojnika, kar je način okvare modelnega potega za vlogo brata ali sestre že zadet."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``services.volume-2-local.snapshot_mode`` (declared in ``meta/services.yml``, overridable per host from the inventory) decides whether a run uses baudolo’s ``--snapshot`` mode. **Quote the value** — YAML reads a bare ``off``/``no``/``false`` as a boolean, and the deploy asserts on the result."
msgstr "``services.volume-2-local.snapshot_mode`` (prijavljeno v ``meta/services.yml``, preobremenjen na gostitelja iz inventarja) odloči, ali run uporablja baudolo’ ``--snapshot`` način. **Navedi vrednost** - YAML bere golo ``off``/``no``/``false`` kot boolean, in razporeditev trdi o rezultatu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``set hostname to {{ inventory_hostname }}`` Applies the desired hostname."
msgstr "``set hostname to {{ inventory_hostname }}`` Uporabi želeno ime gostitelja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``setdefault`` falls back to the supplied value only when the process env has no non-empty value for the key. ``set`` is unconditional. ``get`` reads from the builder, falling back to the process env so derived values (e.g. ``INFINITO_CONTAINER``) can be composed off previously-set keys."
msgstr "``setdefault`` se vrne na dobavljeno vrednost le, če env postopka nima neprazne vrednosti za ključ. ``set`` je brezpogojna. ``get`` bere od graditelja, pada nazaj na proces env tako izpeljane vrednosti (Npr. ``INFINITO_CONTAINER``) se lahko sestavi iz predhodno nastavljenih ključev."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``source_url``:      upstream documentation or source of the MCP surface."
msgstr "``source_url``: dokumentacija v zgornjem toku ali vir površine MCP."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``source``         for binds / configs / secrets, ``''`` if absent"
msgstr "``source`` za vezi / configs / skrivnosti, ``''`` če manjka"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``src``: source path (original location)"
msgstr "``src``: izhodna pot (Prvotna lokacija)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``sse``, so no flow can spawn a local stdio command"
msgstr "``sse``, tako da noben tok ne more drstiti lokalno stdio ukaz"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``state`` is the raw effective outcome ('success' / 'failure' / 'running' / 'cancelled' / ...). Modes without a job are simply absent. A role's variant shards run as separate jobs per mode; the mode state aggregates them worst-first, so one green shard can never mask a failed sibling (gitlab swarm variant 1 red, variant 0 green -> swarm failure)."
msgstr "``state`` je neobdelan učinkovit rezultat ('success' / 'failure' / 'running' / 'cancelled' / ...). Načini brez službe so preprosto odsotni. Različice vloge delujejo kot ločena opravila na način; način stanje jih združuje najslabše-prvi, tako da en zeleni drobec nikoli ne more prikriti propadlega brata ali sestre (varianta gitlab roja 1 rdeča, varianta 0 zelena -> izpad roja)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``str()`` drops the ``TrustedAsTemplate`` tag the loader attached, and the templar returns an untagged string unrendered. Re-tagging before templating is what every sibling lookup does; without it this function would trade the daemon's parse error for its own."
msgstr "``str()`` zmanjša ``TrustedAsTemplate`` označite nalagalnik priključen, in templar vrne neoznačeno struno nepopravljeno. Ponovno označevanje pred skušnjavo je tisto, kar počne vsak brat ali sestra; brez nje bi ta funkcija trgovino demon je parse napake za svoje."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``streamable_http`` (stateless); SSE is not served"
msgstr "``streamable_http`` (brez državljanstva); SSE ni vročena"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``streamable_http`` at ``http://baserowmcp:<http>/mcp``"
msgstr "``streamable_http`` na dan ``http://baserowmcp:<http>/mcp``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``subject`` (mapping): DN fields (C/O/OU/CN)"
msgstr "``subject`` (kartiranje): Polja DN (C/O/OU/CN)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``supported_transports`` / ``supported_auths``: what a client can present."
msgstr "``supported_transports`` / ``supported_auths``: kaj lahko stranka predstavi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``svc-db-openldap`` — for LDAP group synchronization"
msgstr "``svc-db-openldap`` — za sinhronizacijo skupine LDAP"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``svc-db-redis`` (DB 0)"
msgstr "``svc-db-redis`` (DB 0)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``svc-db-redis`` (DB 1)"
msgstr "``svc-db-redis`` (DB 1)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``svc-db-redis`` (DB 2)"
msgstr "``svc-db-redis`` (DB 2)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``svc-db-redis`` (role-local sidecar, service name ``redis``)"
msgstr "``svc-db-redis`` (lokalna prikolica, ime storitve ``redis``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``svc-swarm-manager`` (subset marker), ``svc-storage-nfs-client`` (no ``application_id``), ``svc-registry-docker`` (consumed by the swarm handler that pushes locally-built images, but not declared as a meta-dep so it stays out of compose-mode deploys) are added explicitly because the dep-walker only knows roles that are in the ``applications`` dict. The DR-drill backup roles arrive implicitly: the apps' ``container_backup`` service declaration pulls ``svc-bkp-volume-2-local`` into the closure, and ``svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`` deploys via its group membership on the NFS server host (``extend_inventory``) through the group-driven role includes."
msgstr "``svc-swarm-manager`` (podvrsta označevalec), ``svc-storage-nfs-client`` (ni ``application_id``), ``svc-registry-docker`` (, ki ga uporablja rojev, ki potiska lokalno zgrajene slike, vendar ni deklariran kot meta-dep, tako da ostane izven kompozicije-mode uporablja) so izrecno dodani, ker Dep-walker pozna le vloge, ki so v ``applications`` Dikt. Rezervne vloge DR-drill prihajajo implicitno: aplikacije ``container_backup`` Servisna deklaracija ``svc-bkp-volume-2-local`` v zaprtje in ``svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`` razporedi preko svoje skupine na strežniku NFS (``extend_inventory``) z vlogo, ki jo vodi skupina."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``sys-svc-mail-msmtp``: msmtp client and sendmail replacement"
msgstr "``sys-svc-mail-msmtp``: msmtp odjemalec in sendmail zamenjava"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``sys-svc-mail``: central mail orchestration"
msgstr "``sys-svc-mail``: centralna pošta orkestracija"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``sys-token-store`` is a lightweight Ansible helper role for **resolving and persisting per-user application tokens** in a unified and idempotent way."
msgstr "``sys-token-store`` je lahka Ansible pomočnik vlogo za **žetoni za reševanje in vztrajanje na uporabnika** na enoten in navidezen način."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``sys_token_store_token`` (must be non-empty)"
msgstr "``sys_token_store_token`` (mora biti neprazno)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``system_service_run_list`` (list): list of systemd unit names to run"
msgstr "``system_service_run_list`` (seznam): seznam sistemskih imen enot za zagon"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``systemctl list-units`` reports a forking unit as active/running while its guessed main process is gone, and the containers carry no ``ps``, so the unit table alone cannot answer whether a daemon is still there. MainPID and NRestarts can."
msgstr "``systemctl list-units`` poroča kovaško enoto kot aktivno/tekoče, medtem ko je njen ugibani glavni proces izginil, in zabojniki nosijo do ``ps``, Zato tabela ne more odgovoriti, ali je demon še vedno tam. MainPID in NRestarts lahko."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``target``         the one container path this entry mounts at, present"
msgstr "``target`` ena pot zabojnika, na kateri je ta vstopni priključek"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``target`` is the host to restore onto (``localhost`` = local); a remote host makes the recover push over ssh (rsync target / docker host / secret paths gain the remote prefix)."
msgstr "``target`` je gostitelj za obnovitev na (``localhost`` = lokalno); oddaljen gostitelj naredi okrevanje potiska čez ssh (rsync cilj / docker gostitelj / skrivne poti pridobijo oddaljeno predpono)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``target`` is what lets ``meta/volumes.yml`` stay the single source of a container path: a role defines its constant from the registry"
msgstr "``target`` To je tisto, kar smo ``meta/volumes.yml`` ohraniti en sam vir poti zabojnika: vloga določa njegovo konstanto iz registra"

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``targets``        ``{service: container path}`` built from ``mounts``"
msgstr "``targets`` ``{service: container path}`` izdelani iz ``mounts``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``tasks/01_manager_ops.yml`` therefore rewrites ``curlsecurityblockedhosts`` to ``MOODLE_EGRESS_BLOCKED_HOSTS`` and extends ``curlsecurityallowedport`` with the port of ``MOODLE_LITELLM_CHAT_ENDPOINT`` when the ``litellm`` service is enabled. Loopback, ``0.0.0.0`` and the cloud metadata address stay blocked; the RFC1918 ranges are opened. The Docker address pool and the bridge gateway that serves the pinned Keycloak authority both live inside them."
msgstr "``tasks/01_manager_ops.yml`` zato se spremeni ``curlsecurityblockedhosts`` do ``MOODLE_EGRESS_BLOCKED_HOSTS`` in razširi ``curlsecurityallowedport`` s pristaniščem ``MOODLE_LITELLM_CHAT_ENDPOINT`` ko ``litellm`` storitev je omogočena. Zanka. ``0.0.0.0`` in naslov metapodatkov o oblaku ostane blokiran; RFC1918 Razponi so odprti. Docker naslov bazen in most vrata, ki služi pripete Keycloak Oba živita v njih."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``tasks/utils/`` is the repository’s home for unnumbered, includable task files, so the entrypoint carries no step number."
msgstr "``tasks/utils/`` je dom skladišča za neštevilčne, zložljive datoteke opravil, zato vnosna točka ne nosi številke koraka."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``tcp``, ``udp``, or a list of both. One list item per transport. Omit for compose's own default, which publishes no suffix."
msgstr "``tcp``, ``udp``, ali seznam obeh. En seznam na prevoz. Omit za komponiranje lastnega privzetega, ki objavlja brez pripone."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``templates/package.json.j2``: ``@playwright/test`` version derived from ``meta/services.yml.playwright.version``"
msgstr "``templates/package.json.j2``: ``@playwright/test`` Različica, izpeljana iz ``meta/services.yml.playwright.version``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``templates/playwright.env.j2`` acts as the stable marker for discovery and as the source of environment configuration."
msgstr "``templates/playwright.env.j2`` deluje kot stabilen označevalec za odkritje in kot vir konfiguracije okolja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``templates/roles/README.md.j2.tmpl`` is the single source of truth for the role-README structure. :mod:`cli.build.docs.readme.schema` derives the required/optional section set from it; the lint (``tests/lint/ansible/roles/test_readme.py``) and the generator (``python -m cli.build.docs.readme``) both consume that same schema so the three never drift."
msgstr "``templates/roles/README.md.j2.tmpl`` je edini vir resnice za strukturo vloge-README. :mod:`cli.build.docs.readme.schema` iz nje izhaja zahtevani/neobvezni del; (``tests/lint/ansible/roles/test_readme.py``) in generatorjem (``python -m cli.build.docs.readme``) Oba zaužijeta isto shemo, tako da trije nikoli ne zaidejo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, no-python-format, python-brace-format
msgid "``templates/roles/README.md.j2.tmpl`` is the single source of truth. The required sections are the H2s the template emits with no optional context; the optional sections are the extra H2s that appear once every ``{% if ... %}``-guarded variable is supplied. Rendering the template both ways and diffing the H2 sets keeps the lint and the generator in lock-step with the template."
msgstr "``templates/roles/README.md.j2.tmpl`` je edini vir resnice. Zahtevani odseki so H2s predloga oddaja brez izbirnega konteksta; neobvezni odseki so dodatni H2s, ki se pojavijo enkrat ``{% if ... %}``-Zavarovana spremenljivka je na voljo. Ponarejanje predloge v obe smeri in diffing H2 sets ohranja lint in generator v zaklepa korak s predlogo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``test-bridge-roster.js`` probes the Synapse ``/_matrix/client/v3/profile/{bot}`` endpoint for every enabled bridge and fails on 5xx (skipped when no bridge is enabled)."
msgstr "``test-bridge-roster.js`` sonde Synapse ``/_matrix/client/v3/profile/{bot}`` končna točka za vsak omogočen most in neuspešen 5xx (preskoči, ko most ni omogočen)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``test-element-call.js`` opens the Element home view and verifies a call-widget control surfaces when ``services.matrix.conferencing.element_call=true`` (skipped otherwise)."
msgstr "``test-element-call.js`` odpre pogled na dom Elementa in preveri nadzorne površine klicne widget, ko ``services.matrix.conferencing.element_call=true`` (preskoči drugače)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``test-login-ldap-admin.js`` — OpenLDAP bind, administrator."
msgstr "``test-login-ldap-admin.js`` — OpenLDAP Zaveži, administrator."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``test-login-ldap-biber.js`` — OpenLDAP bind, ``biber`` (non-admin RBAC)."
msgstr "``test-login-ldap-biber.js`` — OpenLDAP vezava, ``biber`` (RBAC, ki ni admin)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``test-login-native.js`` — administrator native (local password) login; skipped when ``sso`` is enabled (native login is disabled under OIDC)."
msgstr "``test-login-native.js`` — skrbnik domorodec (krajevno geslo) prijava; preskoči kadar ``sso`` je omogočeno (Narojena prijava je onemogočena pod OIDC)."

