# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh api` switches implicitly from GET to POST as soon as a body-flag is present; no explicit `-X`/`--method` is required. Without these ask rules the broad `Bash(*)` allow would let body-carrying `gh api` POSTs through silently. Short forms (`-f`, `-F`), long forms (`--field`, `--raw-field`), and file input (`--input`) are all listed so no spelling slips past. A future gh-CLI body-flag would need to be added here explicitly."
msgstr "`gh api` implicitno preklopi iz GET v POST takoj, ko je prisotna zanka za telo; ni izrecno `-X`/`--method` se zahteva. Brez tega vprašajte po pravilih. `Bash(*)` dopustno bi bilo, da se prenaša telo `gh api` POSTI skozi molče. Kratke oblike (`-f`, `-F`), dolge oblike (`--field`, `--raw-field`), in vnos datoteke (`--input`) Vsi so na seznamu, tako da ni črkovanja mimo. Prihodnjo gh-CLI telo-flag bi bilo treba dodati tukaj izrecno."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh config set editor /tmp/evil.sh` plants a binary that runs the next time any `gh` subcommand opens an editor (e.g. `gh issue create` without `--body`), a deferred-execution backdoor that survives the current session. Persistent CLI config belongs to a deliberate operator decision."
msgstr "`gh config set editor /tmp/evil.sh` rastline binarno, ki teče naslednjič `gh` podukaz odpre urejevalnik (Npr. `gh issue create` brez `--body`), odložena-izvršitev zadnja vrata, ki preživi trenutno sejo. Vztrajni konfig CLI pripada namerni odločitvi operaterja."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh workflow run` does NOT print the new run id. Resolve it by repeating the same list query until the returned databaseId is non-empty AND differs from `<prev-run-id>`. That value is `<run-id>`. Each repeat MUST be a separate tool invocation; no shell loop. Do NOT accept a result equal to `<prev-run-id>`; that would attach the watcher to the stale run and return its old exit status immediately."
msgstr "`gh workflow run` ne natisne novega zagnanega ID. Rešite ga tako, da ponovite isto poizvedbo seznama, dokler vrnjena zbirka podatkovId ni prazna IN se razlikuje od `<prev-run-id>`. Ta vrednost je `<run-id>`. Vsaka ponovitev MORA biti ločeno orodje poziv; brez lupinske zanke. NE sprejmi rezultata, ki je enak `<prev-run-id>`; ki bi priključiti opazovalec na zastoj teči in vrniti svoj stari status izhoda takoj."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "`gh` CLI's cache directory (HTTP response cache + extension metadata). Granted because every `gh` invocation writes cache entries at startup; denying it would require every `gh` call to be wrapped with an `XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/...` env prefix, which adds a shell shape that falls out of sandbox auto-allow and forces per-subcommand allow entries. Auth tokens are **not** stored here (they live in `~/.config/gh/`, which stays read-only). Persistence trade-off is identical to `~/.cache/pip` / `~/.cache/pre-commit`: cache poisoning, if it occurred, would survive reboots, but API auth is server-side so the blast radius is bounded to wrong-output-to-operator."
msgstr "`gh` Imenik predpomnilnika CLI (Predpomnilnik odzivov HTTP + razširitveni metapodatki). Seveda, ker vsak `gh` invokacija ob zagonu piše predpomnilniške vnose; zanikanje bi zahtevalo vse `gh` klic, da se zaviti z `XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/...` env predpona, ki dodaja obliko lupine, ki pade iz sandbox avto-dopust in sile na podpoveljnika omogočajo vstop. Žetoni za avte so **ni** shranjeno tukaj (živijo v `~/.config/gh/`, ki ostane samo za branje). Vztrajen kompromis je enak `~/.cache/pip` / `~/.cache/pre-commit`: Zastrupitev predpomnilnika, če se je zgodilo, bi preživel reboots, vendar API je strežniška stran, zato je radij eksplozije omejen na napačno izhodno napravo."

